0
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
BLACK SCREEN

1
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,460
Lumos Maxima.

2
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:41,500
Lumos Maxima.

3
00:01:01,390 --> 00:01:03,210
Lumos Maxima.

4
00:01:05,290 --> 00:01:07,390
Lumos Maxima.

5
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:11,260
Lumos Maxima!

6
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:42,630
Harry. Harry.

7
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:44,830
Harry, open the door.

8
00:01:51,510 --> 00:01:54,010
Marge. How lovely to see...

9
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:57,540
Uncle Vernon, I need you to sign this form.

10
00:01:57,550 --> 00:01:59,050
What is it?

11
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:01,350
Nothing. School stuff.

12
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:04,180
Later perhaps, if you behave.

13
00:02:04,190 --> 00:02:06,550
I will if she does.

14
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:09,930
-Oh, you're still here, are you?   -Yes.

15
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,890
Don't say yes in that ungrateful way.

16
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:15,030
Damn good of my brother to keep you.

17
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:19,530
He'd have been straight to an orphanage if he'd been dumped on my doorstep.

18
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:24,070
Is that my Dudders? Is that my little neffy-pooh?

19
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:26,040
Give us a kiss. Come on. Up, up.

20
00:02:26,050 --> 00:02:28,470
Take Marge's suitcase upstairs.

21
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:30,710
Okay.

22
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:36,960
Finish that off for Mommy. Good boy, Rippy-pooh.

23
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:40,890
-Can I tempt you, Marge?   -Just a small one.

24
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:44,030
Excellent nosh, Petunia.

25
00:02:44,430 --> 00:02:46,620
A bit more.

26
00:02:46,970 --> 00:02:50,500
Usually just a fry-up for me, what with 1 2 dogs.

27
00:02:50,510 --> 00:02:53,300
Just a bit more. That's a boy.

28
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:58,340
You wanna try a little drop of brandy?

29
00:02:58,350 --> 00:03:02,570
A little drop of brandy-brandy windy-wandy for Rippy-pippy-pooh?

30
00:03:03,890 --> 00:03:05,840
What are you smirking at?

31
00:03:05,850 --> 00:03:07,880
Where did you send the boy, Vernon?

32
00:03:07,890 --> 00:03:11,350
St. Brutus'. It's a fine institution for hopeless cases.

33
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:14,590
Do they use a cane at St. Brutus', boy?

34
00:03:17,830 --> 00:03:19,220
Oh, yeah.

35
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:22,190
Yeah. I've been beaten loads of times.

36
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,960
Excellent. I won't have this namby-pamby...

37
00:03:24,970 --> 00:03:28,300
...wishy-washy nonsense about not beating people who deserve it.

38
00:03:28,310 --> 00:03:31,570
You mustn't blame yourself about how this one turned out.

39
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:33,230
It's all to do with blood.

40
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:35,670
Bad blood will out.

41
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:38,010
What is it the boy's father did, Petunia?

42
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:41,180
Nothing. He didn't work. He was unemployed.

43
00:03:41,190 --> 00:03:44,180
-And a drunk too, no doubt?   -That's a lie.

44
00:03:44,190 --> 00:03:46,950
-What did you say?   -My dad wasn't a drunk.

45
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:51,420
Don't worry. Don't fuss,

46
00:03:51,430 --> 00:03:53,990
Petunia. I have a very firm grip.

47
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,990
I think it's time you went to bed.

48
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,430
Quiet, Vernon. You, clean it up.

49
00:04:00,410 --> 00:04:03,600
Actually, it's nothing to do with the father.

50
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:07,740
It's all to do with the mother. You see it all the time with dogs.

51
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:09,680
If something's wrong with the bitch,

52
00:04:09,690 --> 00:04:11,980
then something's wrong with the pup.

53
00:04:11,990 --> 00:04:13,880
Shut up! Shut up!

54
00:04:18,690 --> 00:04:20,590
Right.

55
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,920
Let me tell you...

56
00:04:44,190 --> 00:04:46,510
Vernon!

57
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:51,350
Vernon! Vernon, do something!

58
00:05:34,570 --> 00:05:36,790
Stop!

59
00:05:39,170 --> 00:05:41,930
I've got you, Marge. I've got you.

60
00:05:45,150 --> 00:05:47,370
-Hold on, hold on.   -Get off.

61
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:50,450
-Don't you dare!   -Sorry.

62
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:53,410
Oh, Vernon.

63
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:55,310
Oh, God.

64
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:57,320
Marge!

65
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,630
Please!

66
00:06:07,030 --> 00:06:09,430
Marge!

67
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:13,700
Come back!

68
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:40,060
You bring her back! You bring her back now.

69
00:06:40,070 --> 00:06:43,530
-You put her right!   -No. She deserved what she got.

70
00:06:43,770 --> 00:06:44,930
-Keep away from me.

71
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:47,100
-You can't do magic outside school.

72
00:06:47,110 --> 00:06:50,270
-Yeah? Try me.   -They won't let you back now.

73
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,770
You've nowhere to go.

74
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:54,310
I don't care. Anywhere is better than here.

75
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:32,270
Welcome to the Knight Bus...

76
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:35,800
...emergency transport for the stranded witch or wizard.

77
00:08:35,810 --> 00:08:38,180
My name is Stan Shunpike,

78
00:08:38,190 --> 00:08:40,970
and I will be your conductor for this evening.

79
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:46,160
What you doing down there?

80
00:08:46,690 --> 00:08:49,050
-I fell over.   -What you fell over for?

81
00:08:49,060 --> 00:08:50,310
-I didn't do it on purpose.

82
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:51,890
-Well, come on, then.

83
00:08:51,930 --> 00:08:54,290
Let's not wait for the grass to grow.

84
00:09:01,210 --> 00:09:04,430
-What you looking at?   -Nothing.

85
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:06,340
Well, come on, then. In.

86
00:09:06,350 --> 00:09:09,380
No, no, no. I'll get this. You get in.

87
00:09:14,150 --> 00:09:16,550
Come on.

88
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:29,190
Come on. Move on, move on.

89
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:47,180
-Take her away, Ern.   -Yeah, take it away, Ernie.

90
00:09:47,190 --> 00:09:49,620
It's going to be a bumpy ride.

91
00:10:00,130 --> 00:10:03,600
-What did you say your name was?   -I didn't.

92
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:08,260
-Whereabouts are you headed?   -The Leaky Cauldron. That's in London.

93
00:10:08,310 --> 00:10:11,400
You hear that? "The Leaky Cauldron. That's in London."

94
00:10:11,410 --> 00:10:13,900
The Leaky Cauldron. If you have pea soup...

95
00:10:13,910 --> 00:10:16,910
...make sure you eat it before it eats you.

96
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:22,910
-But the Muggles. Can't they see us?   -Muggles?

97
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:24,810
They don't see nothing, do they?

98
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:26,510
No, but if you jab them with a fork,

99
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:27,580
they feel.

100
00:10:29,130 --> 00:10:32,390
Ernie, little old lady at 1 2 o'clock!

101
00:10:40,910 --> 00:10:43,630
10  9  8...
Ten, nine, eight...

102
00:10:43,670 --> 00:10:46,570
...7  6  5...
...seven, six, five...

103
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:49,010
...4  3  3.5...
...four, three, three and a half...

104
00:10:49,050 --> 00:10:51,010
...2  1.75
...two, one and three quarters.

105
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:53,170
Yes!

106
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,920
Who is that?

107
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:01,490
That man.

108
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,960
Who is that?

109
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:06,650
Who is...?

110
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:09,260
That is Sirius Black, that is.

111
00:11:09,630 --> 00:11:13,100
Don't tell me you've never been hearing of Sirius Black.

112
00:11:14,210 --> 00:11:16,630
He's a murderer.

113
00:11:16,640 --> 00:11:19,470
Got himself locked up in Azkaban for it.

114
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:21,130
-How did he escape?

115
00:11:21,140 --> 00:11:23,500
-Well, that's the question, isn't it?

116
00:11:23,510 --> 00:11:25,680
He's the first one that done it.

117
00:11:26,450 --> 00:11:31,280
He was a big supporter of You-Know-Who.

118
00:11:31,790 --> 00:11:33,810
I reckon you've heard of him.

119
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:35,580
Yeah.

120
00:11:35,590 --> 00:11:37,120
Him I've heard of.

121
00:11:39,630 --> 00:11:42,490
Ernie, two double-deckers at 1 2 o'clock.

122
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:44,660
They're getting closer, Ernie.

123
00:11:45,270 --> 00:11:47,700
Ernie, they're right on top of us!

124
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:57,510
Mind your head.

125
00:12:02,190 --> 00:12:04,350
Hey, guys? Guys?

126
00:12:04,350 --> 00:12:06,710
Why the long faces?

127
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:15,000
Yeah, yeah. Nearly there. Nearly there.

128
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:23,800
-The Leaky Cauldron.   -Next stop, Knockturn Alley.

129
00:12:24,940 --> 00:12:27,800
Mr. Potter, at last.

130
00:12:30,610 --> 00:12:33,540
-Take it away, Ern.   -Yeah, take it away, Ernie!

131
00:12:56,540 --> 00:12:58,570
Room 11.

132
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:02,440
Hedwig.

133
00:13:02,450 --> 00:13:05,440
Right smart bird you got there, Mr. Potter.

134
00:13:05,450 --> 00:13:09,340
He arrived here just five minutes before yourself.

135
00:13:11,050 --> 00:13:12,250
As Minister for Magic,

136
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:14,850
it is my duty to inform you, Mr. Potter...

137
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:18,220
...earlier this evening your uncle's sister was located...

138
00:13:18,230 --> 00:13:22,360
...a little south of Sheffield, circling a chimney stack.

139
00:13:22,370 --> 00:13:26,260
The Accidental Magic Reversal Department was dispatched immediately.

140
00:13:26,270 --> 00:13:31,270
She has been properly punctured and her memory modified.

141
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:36,140
She will have no recollection of the incident whatsoever.

142
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:38,900
So that's that...

143
00:13:38,910 --> 00:13:41,980
...and no harm done.

144
00:13:42,450 --> 00:13:43,940
Pea soup?

145
00:13:43,950 --> 00:13:46,250
No, thank you.

146
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:48,610
-Minister?   -Yes?

147
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,550
-I don't understand.   -Understand?

148
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:51,680
I broke the law.

149
00:13:51,690 --> 00:13:54,290
Underage wizards can't use magic at home.

150
00:13:54,330 --> 00:13:57,490
Come now. The Ministry doesn't send people to Azkaban...

151
00:13:57,500 --> 00:14:00,220
...for blowing up their aunts.

152
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:08,700
On the other hand, running away like that, given the state of things...

153
00:14:08,710 --> 00:14:11,380
...was very, very irresponsible.

154
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:12,960
-"The state of things," sir?

155
00:14:12,970 --> 00:14:15,310
-We have a killer on the loose.

156
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:17,310
Sirius Black, you mean?

157
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:19,280
But what's he got to do with me?

158
00:14:21,390 --> 00:14:26,390
Nothing, of course. You're safe. And that's what matters.

159
00:14:26,430 --> 00:14:29,690
And tomorrow you'll be on your way back to Hogwarts.

160
00:14:29,700 --> 00:14:32,830
These are your new schoolbooks. I took the liberty...

161
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:37,030
...of having them brought here. Now Tom will show you to your room.

162
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:43,240
Hedwig.

163
00:14:43,310 --> 00:14:46,810
Oh, by the way, Harry.

164
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:51,180
Whilst you're here, it would be best if you didn't wander.

165
00:14:52,550 --> 00:14:55,650
Right! You gonna move that bus or what?

166
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:16,460
Housekeeping.

167
00:16:19,710 --> 00:16:22,140
I'll come back later.

168
00:16:29,550 --> 00:16:31,110
I'm warning you, Hermione.

169
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:32,820
Keep that beast away from Scabbers,

170
00:16:32,830 --> 00:16:35,010
or I'll turn it into a tea cozy.

171
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:37,250
It's a cat, Ronald. What do you expect?

172
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:38,280
-It's in his nature.

173
00:16:38,290 --> 00:16:40,420
-A cat? Is that what they told you?

174
00:16:40,430 --> 00:16:42,940
Looks like a pig with hair.

175
00:16:42,950 --> 00:16:44,150
That's rich coming from the owner

176
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:45,820
of that smelly old shoe brush.

177
00:16:45,830 --> 00:16:48,490
Crookshanks, just ignore the mean little boy.

178
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:50,260
Harry.

179
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:52,770
Harry.

180
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:57,000
-Egypt. What's it like?   -Brilliant. Loads of old stuff...

181
00:16:57,040 --> 00:17:00,540
...Iike mummies, tombs, even Scabbers enjoyed himself.

182
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:03,910
-Egyptians used to worship cats. -Along with the dung beetle.

183
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:07,250
-Not flashing that clipping again?   -I haven't shown anyone.

184
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:09,810
No, not a soul. Not unless you count Tom.

185
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:11,420
-The day maid.   -Night maid.

186
00:17:11,430 --> 00:17:13,680
-Cook.   -The bloke who fixed the toilet.

187
00:17:13,690 --> 00:17:15,290
-Harry.   -Mrs. Weasley.

188
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:17,620
-Good to see you, dear.   -Good to see you.

189
00:17:17,630 --> 00:17:19,120
-Got everything?   -Yes.

190
00:17:19,130 --> 00:17:21,460
-Yes? All your books?   -It's all upstairs.

191
00:17:21,470 --> 00:17:23,070
-Your clothes?   -Everything.

192
00:17:23,070 --> 00:17:24,460
-Good boy.   -Thank you.

193
00:17:24,470 --> 00:17:26,660
-Harry Potter.   -Mr. Weasley.

194
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:28,980
-Harry, wonder if I might have a word?

195
00:17:28,990 --> 00:17:30,360
-Yeah, sure.

196
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:33,170
-Hermione.   -Good morning, Mr. Weasley.

197
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:37,010
-Looking forward to a new term?   -Yeah. It should be great.

198
00:17:39,890 --> 00:17:43,880
Harry, some within the Ministry would strongly discourage me...

199
00:17:43,890 --> 00:17:46,720
...from divulging what I'm about to reveal to you.

200
00:17:46,730 --> 00:17:50,220
But I think that you need to know the facts.

201
00:17:50,230 --> 00:17:53,020
You are in danger.

202
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:56,170
Grave danger.

203
00:17:56,470 --> 00:17:59,300
Has this anything to do with Sirius Black, sir?

204
00:17:59,910 --> 00:18:02,470
What do you know about Sirius Black, Harry?

205
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:04,770
-Only that he's escaped from Azkaban.

206
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:06,370
-Do you know why?

207
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:09,840
Thirteen years ago, when you stopped...

208
00:18:09,850 --> 00:18:11,840
-Voldemort.   -Don't say his name.

209
00:18:11,850 --> 00:18:13,340
Sorry.

210
00:18:13,350 --> 00:18:16,410
When you stopped You-Know-Who...

211
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:18,210
...Black lost everything.

212
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:22,690
But to this day, he still remains a faithful servant.

213
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:25,020
And in his mind...

214
00:18:25,030 --> 00:18:28,190
...you are the only thing that stands in the way...

215
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:32,130
...of You-Know-Who returning to power.

216
00:18:32,140 --> 00:18:34,430
And that is why...

217
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:37,200
...he has escaped from Azkaban.

218
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:39,240
To find you.

219
00:18:40,510 --> 00:18:42,340
And kill me.

220
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:45,910
Harry, swear to me that whatever you might hear...

221
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:48,640
...you won't go looking for Black.

222
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:50,350
Mr. Weasley...

223
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:54,550
...why would I go looking for someone who wants to kill me?

224
00:18:55,130 --> 00:18:57,050
Quick. Quick.

225
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:59,090
Ron, Ron!

226
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:01,890
Oh, for goodness'sake!

227
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:04,570
Don't lose him!

228
00:19:05,410 --> 00:19:07,660
I didn't mean to blow her up. I just...

229
00:19:07,670 --> 00:19:10,270
-I lost control.   -Brilliant.

230
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:12,230
-Honestly, Ron, it's not funny.

231
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:14,040
-Harry was lucky not to be expelled.

232
00:19:14,050 --> 00:19:15,940
I was lucky not to be arrested.

233
00:19:15,950 --> 00:19:18,170
I still think it was brilliant.

234
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:21,120
Come on. Everywhere else is full.

235
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:25,280
Who do you think that is?

236
00:19:25,290 --> 00:19:28,320
-Professor R.J. Lupin.   -Do you know everything?

237
00:19:28,330 --> 00:19:30,620
How is it she knows everything?

238
00:19:30,630 --> 00:19:33,960
-It's on his suitcase, Ronald.   -Oh.

239
00:19:34,070 --> 00:19:35,750
-Do you think he's really asleep?

240
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:37,530
-Seems to be. Why?

241
00:19:39,070 --> 00:19:41,400
I gotta tell you something.

242
00:19:54,650 --> 00:19:55,850
Let me get this straight.

243
00:19:55,860 --> 00:19:58,050
Sirius Black escaped from Azkaban...

244
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:00,150
-...to come after you?   -Yeah.

245
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:02,220
But they'll catch Black, won't they?

246
00:20:02,230 --> 00:20:05,190
-I mean, everyone's looking for him.   -Sure.

247
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:08,690
Except no one's ever broken out of Azkaban before...

248
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:12,730
-...and he's a murderous, raving lunatic.   -Thanks, Ron.

249
00:20:14,010 --> 00:20:15,800
Why are we stopping?

250
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:18,600
We can't be there yet.

251
00:20:22,610 --> 00:20:25,080
What's going on?

252
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:27,950
I don't know. Maybe we've broken down.

253
00:20:29,690 --> 00:20:32,220
Ouch, Ron. That was my foot.

254
00:20:32,890 --> 00:20:35,020
There's something moving out there.

255
00:20:48,410 --> 00:20:51,630
I think someone's coming aboard.

256
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:19,700
Bloody hell! What's happening?

257
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:33,240
Harry.

258
00:22:34,150 --> 00:22:36,180
Harry, are you all right?

259
00:22:42,150 --> 00:22:44,010
Thank you.

260
00:22:44,990 --> 00:22:47,620
Here, eat this. It'll help.

261
00:22:47,930 --> 00:22:50,250
It's all right. It's chocolate.

262
00:22:56,370 --> 00:22:58,590
What was that thing that came?

263
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:02,200
It was a dementor. One of the guards of Azkaban. It's gone now.

264
00:23:02,210 --> 00:23:05,070
It was searching the train for Sirius Black.

265
00:23:05,080 --> 00:23:08,900
If you'll excuse me, I need to have a little word with the driver.

266
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:16,420
Eat. You'll feel better.

267
00:23:22,030 --> 00:23:23,520
What happened to me?

268
00:23:23,530 --> 00:23:25,420
Well, you sort of went rigid.

269
00:23:25,430 --> 00:23:28,790
We thought maybe you were having a fit or something.

270
00:23:30,370 --> 00:23:32,330
And did either of you two...

271
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:33,830
...you know...

272
00:23:33,840 --> 00:23:37,060
-...pass out?   -No.

273
00:23:37,070 --> 00:23:38,930
I felt weird, though.

274
00:23:38,940 --> 00:23:40,970
Like I'd never be cheerful again.

275
00:23:42,050 --> 00:23:44,400
But someone was screaming.

276
00:23:44,410 --> 00:23:45,980
A woman.

277
00:23:46,750 --> 00:23:48,940
No one was screaming, Harry.

278
00:24:47,940 --> 00:24:52,000
Welcome! Welcome to another year at Hogwarts.

279
00:24:52,010 --> 00:24:54,210
Now, I'd like to say a few words...

280
00:24:54,220 --> 00:24:58,710
...before we all become too befuddled by our excellent feast.

281
00:24:58,720 --> 00:25:02,180
First, I'm pleased to welcome Professor R.J. Lupin...

282
00:25:02,190 --> 00:25:04,820
...who's kindly consented to fill the post...

283
00:25:04,830 --> 00:25:07,450
...of Defense Against the Dark Arts teacher.

284
00:25:07,460 --> 00:25:10,190
Good luck, professor.

285
00:25:14,600 --> 00:25:18,100
Of course. That's why he knew to give you the chocolate, Harry.

286
00:25:18,110 --> 00:25:20,970
Potter. Is it true you fainted?

287
00:25:21,610 --> 00:25:23,440
-I mean, you actually fainted?

288
00:25:23,450 --> 00:25:24,770
-Shove off, Malfoy.

289
00:25:24,780 --> 00:25:26,940
-How did he find out?   -Just forget it.

290
00:25:26,950 --> 00:25:29,510
Our Care of Magical Creatures teacher...

291
00:25:29,520 --> 00:25:31,580
...has decided to retire...

292
00:25:31,590 --> 00:25:35,520
...in order to spend more time with his remaining limbs.

293
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:38,380
Fortunately, I'm delighted to announce...

294
00:25:38,390 --> 00:25:41,390
...that his place will be taken by none other...

295
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:45,930
...than our own Rubeus Hagrid.

296
00:25:57,010 --> 00:26:00,010
Finally, on a more disquieting note...

297
00:26:00,020 --> 00:26:02,710
...at the request of the Ministry of Magic...

298
00:26:02,720 --> 00:26:08,080
...Hogwarts will, until further notice, play host to the dementors of Azkaban

299
00:26:08,560 --> 00:26:12,210
...until such a time as Sirius Black is captured.

300
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:16,820
The dementors will be stationed at every entrance to the grounds.

301
00:26:16,830 --> 00:26:18,660
Now whilst I've been assured...

302
00:26:18,670 --> 00:26:22,490
...that their presence will not disrupt our day-to-day activities...

303
00:26:22,500 --> 00:26:24,030
...a word of caution.

304
00:26:24,040 --> 00:26:27,370
Dementors are vicious creatures. They'll not distinguish...

305
00:26:27,380 --> 00:26:30,940
...between the one they hunt and the one who gets in their way.

306
00:26:30,950 --> 00:26:34,740
Therefore, I must warn each and every one of you...

307
00:26:34,750 --> 00:26:38,580
...to give them no reason to harm you.

308
00:26:39,150 --> 00:26:44,450
It is not in the nature of a dementor to be forgiving.

309
00:26:46,390 --> 00:26:49,850
But you know, happiness can be found...

310
00:26:49,860 --> 00:26:53,660
...even in the darkest of times...

311
00:26:54,700 --> 00:26:58,770
...if one only remembers to turn on the light.

312
00:27:10,590 --> 00:27:12,780
Fortuna Major.

313
00:27:15,420 --> 00:27:18,280
Here, listen. She just won't let me in.

314
00:27:18,290 --> 00:27:21,390
-Fortuna Major. -No, no. Wait, wait.

315
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:23,430
Watch this.

316
00:27:33,980 --> 00:27:37,730
-Amazing. Just with my voice.

317
00:27:37,740 --> 00:27:39,130
-Fortuna Major.

318
00:27:39,150 --> 00:27:42,910
-Yes, all right. Go in.   -Thank you.

319
00:27:44,720 --> 00:27:46,840
Still doing that after three years.

320
00:27:46,850 --> 00:27:49,210
-She can't even sing.   -Exactly.

321
00:27:50,260 --> 00:27:52,620
-Hey, man.   -Hey, man.

322
00:27:53,460 --> 00:27:55,030
-Oh, God.   -That's awful.

323
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:58,160
Green. That's a monkey.

324
00:27:59,770 --> 00:28:02,590
-What is that?   -You call that a monkey?

325
00:28:02,600 --> 00:28:04,960
Do not give him one again.

326
00:28:04,970 --> 00:28:07,800
Hey, Neville, try an elephant.

327
00:28:14,680 --> 00:28:16,640
-Ron, catch.   -I will.

328
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:23,950
I think we have a winner.

329
00:28:24,690 --> 00:28:27,220
-Oh, don't try one of them.   -Oh, no.

330
00:28:27,660 --> 00:28:30,350
Look at him. His face.

331
00:29:13,810 --> 00:29:16,240
Welcome, my children.

332
00:29:16,240 --> 00:29:21,500
In this room, you shall explore the noble art of Divination.

333
00:29:21,510 --> 00:29:27,020
In this room, you shall discover if you possess the Sight.

334
00:29:28,220 --> 00:29:32,350
Hello. I am Professor Trelawney.

335
00:29:32,360 --> 00:29:37,150
Together we shall cast ourselves into the future.

336
00:29:37,200 --> 00:29:38,870
This term, we'll focus on Tasseomancy,

337
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:41,190
the art of reading tea leaves.

338
00:29:41,200 --> 00:29:44,960
So please, take the cup of the person sitting opposite you.

339
00:29:45,270 --> 00:29:46,840
What do you see?

340
00:29:46,840 --> 00:29:49,900
The truth lies buried like a sentence deep within a book,

341
00:29:49,910 --> 00:29:52,670
waiting to be read.

342
00:29:52,710 --> 00:29:55,270
But first, you must broaden your minds.

343
00:29:55,280 --> 00:29:58,170
-First, you must look beyond.

344
00:29:58,180 --> 00:29:59,980
-What a load of rubbish.

345
00:29:59,990 --> 00:30:02,080
-Where did you come from?   -Me?

346
00:30:02,090 --> 00:30:04,910
-I've been here all this time.   -You, boy...

347
00:30:04,920 --> 00:30:07,420
Is your grandmother quite well?

348
00:30:07,890 --> 00:30:09,490
I think so.

349
00:30:09,500 --> 00:30:12,490
I wouldn't be so sure of that. Give me the cup.

350
00:30:15,300 --> 00:30:16,870
Pity.

351
00:30:16,900 --> 00:30:19,700
Broaden your minds.

352
00:30:23,110 --> 00:30:26,600
Your aura is pulsing, dear. Are you in the beyond?

353
00:30:26,610 --> 00:30:28,710
-I think you are.   -Sure.

354
00:30:28,750 --> 00:30:31,110
Look at the cup. Tell me what you see.

355
00:30:31,120 --> 00:30:33,010
Yeah.

356
00:30:33,650 --> 00:30:38,290
Harry's got sort of a wonky cross. That's trials and suffering.

357
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:42,350
And that there could be the sun and that's happiness.

358
00:30:42,390 --> 00:30:43,890
So...

359
00:30:43,900 --> 00:30:48,120
...you're gonna suffer, but you're gonna be happy about it.

360
00:30:48,130 --> 00:30:49,660
Give me the cup.

361
00:30:52,040 --> 00:30:54,140
Oh, my dear boy.

362
00:30:56,010 --> 00:30:57,870
My dear...

363
00:30:59,340 --> 00:31:02,640
...you have the Grim.

364
00:31:03,280 --> 00:31:05,170
The Grin? What's the Grin?

365
00:31:05,180 --> 00:31:08,210
Not the Grin, you idiot. The Grim.

366
00:31:08,220 --> 00:31:10,610
"Taking form of a giant spectral dog.

367
00:31:10,620 --> 00:31:13,260
It's among the darkest omens in our world.

368
00:31:13,630 --> 00:31:15,450
It's an omen...

369
00:31:15,460 --> 00:31:17,490
...of death."

370
00:31:21,930 --> 00:31:25,830
You don't think that Grim thing's got anything to do with Sirius Black?

371
00:31:25,840 --> 00:31:27,930
Oh, honestly, Ron. If you ask me,

372
00:31:27,940 --> 00:31:29,940
Divination's a woolly discipline.

373
00:31:29,940 --> 00:31:33,740
Now, Ancient Runes, that's a fascinating subject.

374
00:31:33,750 --> 00:31:37,040
Ancient Runes? Exactly how many classes are you taking?

375
00:31:37,050 --> 00:31:38,870
A fair few.

376
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:41,140
Hang on. That's not possible.

377
00:31:41,150 --> 00:31:44,080
Ancient Runes is in the same time as Divination.

378
00:31:44,090 --> 00:31:46,250
You have to be in two classes at once.

379
00:31:46,260 --> 00:31:46,930
Don't be silly.

380
00:31:46,940 --> 00:31:49,820
How could anyone be in two classes at once?

381
00:31:49,830 --> 00:31:54,260
" Broaden your minds. Use your lnner Eye to see the future."

382
00:31:55,230 --> 00:31:57,000
That's it. Come on, now. Come closer.

383
00:31:57,010 --> 00:31:59,360
Less talking, if you don't mind.

384
00:31:59,370 --> 00:32:01,360
I got a real treat for you today.

385
00:32:01,370 --> 00:32:03,560
A great lesson. So follow me.

386
00:32:14,620 --> 00:32:17,880
Right, you lot. Less chattering. Form a group over there.

387
00:32:17,890 --> 00:32:20,550
And open your books to page 49.

388
00:32:20,560 --> 00:32:22,380
Exactly how do we do that?

389
00:32:22,390 --> 00:32:26,460
Just stroke the spine, of course. Goodness me.

390
00:32:35,640 --> 00:32:39,640
-Don't be such a wimp, Longbottom.   -I'm okay. Okay.

391
00:32:43,110 --> 00:32:44,560
-I think they're funny.

392
00:32:44,570 --> 00:32:46,510
-Oh, yeah. Terribly funny.

393
00:32:46,550 --> 00:32:49,220
Witty. God, this place has gone to the dogs.

394
00:32:49,220 --> 00:32:53,080
Wait until Father hears Dumbledore's got this oaf teaching classes.

395
00:32:53,830 --> 00:32:55,360
Shut up, Malfoy.

396
00:33:09,670 --> 00:33:11,930
Dementor! Dementor!

397
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:22,980
-Just ignore him.   -You're supposed to stroke it.

398
00:33:22,990 --> 00:33:24,650
Yeah.

399
00:33:34,670 --> 00:33:37,830
Isn't he beautiful?

400
00:33:37,840 --> 00:33:40,660
Say hello to Buckbeak.

401
00:33:41,070 --> 00:33:43,500
Hagrid, exactly what is that?

402
00:33:43,510 --> 00:33:45,700
That, Ron, is a hippogriff.

403
00:33:45,710 --> 00:33:49,400
First thing you wanna know is they're very proud creatures.

404
00:33:49,450 --> 00:33:53,470
Very easily offended. You do not want to insult a hippogriff.

405
00:33:53,480 --> 00:33:56,380
It may be the last thing you ever do.

406
00:33:56,390 --> 00:33:59,990
Now, who'd like to come and say hello?

407
00:34:02,330 --> 00:34:04,580
Well done, Harry. Well done.

408
00:34:07,200 --> 00:34:08,800
Come on now.

409
00:34:09,130 --> 00:34:10,660
Now...

410
00:34:10,670 --> 00:34:12,260
...you have to let him make the first move.

411
00:34:12,270 --> 00:34:14,530
It's only polite. So...

412
00:34:14,540 --> 00:34:16,600
...step up. Give him a nice bow.

413
00:34:16,640 --> 00:34:19,200
Then you wait and see if he bows back.

414
00:34:19,210 --> 00:34:21,500
If he does, you can go and touch him.

415
00:34:21,510 --> 00:34:24,910
If not... Well, we'll get to that later.

416
00:34:27,380 --> 00:34:29,610
Just make your bow.

417
00:34:31,020 --> 00:34:32,880
Nice and low.

418
00:34:38,030 --> 00:34:39,890
Back off, Harry. Back off.

419
00:34:41,560 --> 00:34:43,250
Keep still.

420
00:34:44,730 --> 00:34:46,920
Keep still.

421
00:34:54,910 --> 00:34:57,120
Well done, Harry. Well done.

422
00:34:57,130 --> 00:34:59,550
Here, you big brute, you.

423
00:35:01,850 --> 00:35:04,580
Right. I think you can go and pat him now.

424
00:35:04,590 --> 00:35:06,620
Go on. Don't be shy.

425
00:35:14,860 --> 00:35:17,500
Nice and slow, now. Nice and slow. Slow.

426
00:35:20,670 --> 00:35:22,270
Not so fast, Harry.

427
00:35:27,180 --> 00:35:30,610
Slow down, Harry. That's it...

428
00:35:30,610 --> 00:35:33,980
Nice and slow. Now let him come to you.

429
00:35:35,690 --> 00:35:38,180
Slowly, now, slowly, slowly...

430
00:35:38,220 --> 00:35:40,180
That's it...

431
00:35:40,620 --> 00:35:42,150
Yes!

432
00:35:42,560 --> 00:35:46,120
Well done! Well done, Harry, well done!

433
00:35:46,130 --> 00:35:48,320
Does he get to fly?

434
00:35:48,330 --> 00:35:50,930
-I think he may let you ride him now.   -What?

435
00:35:50,930 --> 00:35:52,630
-Come on.   -Hey, hey, hey!

436
00:35:52,640 --> 00:35:56,000
Put you over here, just behind the wing joint.

437
00:35:56,470 --> 00:36:01,040
Don't pull out any of his feathers, because he won't thank you for that.

438
00:37:41,810 --> 00:37:45,500
Well done, Harry, and well done, Buckbeak.

439
00:37:45,510 --> 00:37:47,610
That was wicked, Harry!

440
00:37:47,620 --> 00:37:49,210
Oh, please.

441
00:37:49,820 --> 00:37:52,320
Well done, well done.

442
00:37:52,820 --> 00:37:56,220
-How am I doing me first day?   -Brilliant, professor.

443
00:37:59,430 --> 00:38:01,190
You're not dangerous at all,

444
00:38:01,200 --> 00:38:03,820
are you, you great ugly brute!

445
00:38:03,870 --> 00:38:05,430
Malfoy, no...

446
00:38:06,130 --> 00:38:07,800
No!

447
00:38:08,340 --> 00:38:10,130
Buckbeak!

448
00:38:10,140 --> 00:38:12,460
Whoa, whoa, whoa...

449
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:15,440
Whoa! Buckbeak!

450
00:38:16,380 --> 00:38:18,910
Away, you silly creature...

451
00:38:18,910 --> 00:38:22,170
-It's killed me!   -Calm down. It's just a scratch!

452
00:38:22,220 --> 00:38:23,570
Hagrid!

453
00:38:23,580 --> 00:38:28,980
-He has to be taken to the hospital.   -I'm the teacher. I'll do it.

454
00:38:31,860 --> 00:38:34,890
-You're gonna regret this.   -Class dismissed!

455
00:38:34,900 --> 00:38:37,360
You and your bloody chicken!

456
00:39:00,660 --> 00:39:02,880
Does it hurt terribly, Draco?

457
00:39:02,920 --> 00:39:06,920
It comes and it goes. Still, I consider myself lucky.

458
00:39:06,930 --> 00:39:08,710
Madam Pomfrey said another minute

459
00:39:08,720 --> 00:39:10,460
and I could've lost my arm.

460
00:39:10,600 --> 00:39:12,350
-I can't do homework for weeks.

461
00:39:12,360 --> 00:39:13,660
-Listen to the idiot.

462
00:39:13,700 --> 00:39:16,000
-He's really laying it on thick, isn't he?

463
00:39:16,010 --> 00:39:18,170
-At least Hagrid didn't get fired.

464
00:39:18,170 --> 00:39:20,160
I hear Draco's father's furious.

465
00:39:20,170 --> 00:39:22,100
We haven't heard the end of this.

466
00:39:22,110 --> 00:39:24,140
-He's been sighted!   -Who?

467
00:39:24,150 --> 00:39:26,040
Sirius Black!

468
00:39:26,910 --> 00:39:30,110
Dufftown? That's not far from here.

469
00:39:30,320 --> 00:39:33,110
You don't think he'd come to Hogwarts, do you?

470
00:39:33,120 --> 00:39:34,950
-With dementors at every entrance?

471
00:39:34,960 --> 00:39:35,780
-Dementors?

472
00:39:35,790 --> 00:39:37,440
He slipped past them once.

473
00:39:37,450 --> 00:39:39,320
Who's to say he won't do it again?

474
00:39:39,330 --> 00:39:41,750
That's right. Black could be anywhere.

475
00:39:41,760 --> 00:39:44,050
It's like trying to catch smoke.

476
00:39:44,670 --> 00:39:48,030
Like trying to catch smoke with your bare hands.

477
00:40:13,960 --> 00:40:16,220
Intriguing, isn't it?

478
00:40:19,270 --> 00:40:22,190
Would anyone like to venture a guess...

479
00:40:22,200 --> 00:40:24,200
...as to what is inside?

480
00:40:24,200 --> 00:40:28,400
-That's a boggart, that is.   -Very good, Mr. Thomas.

481
00:40:28,980 --> 00:40:32,080
Now, can anybody tell me what a boggart looks like?

482
00:40:32,080 --> 00:40:34,300
-No one knows.   -When did she get here?

483
00:40:34,350 --> 00:40:36,040
Boggarts are shape-shifters.

484
00:40:36,050 --> 00:40:39,450
They take the shape of whatever a person fears the most.

485
00:40:39,490 --> 00:40:41,520
-That's what makes them so...

486
00:40:41,530 --> 00:40:44,090
-So terrifying, yes, yes, yes...

487
00:40:44,090 --> 00:40:49,750
Luckily, a very simple charm exists to repel a boggart.

488
00:40:50,930 --> 00:40:54,900
Let's practice it now. Without wands, please.

489
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:57,690
After me. Riddikulus!

490
00:40:57,700 --> 00:41:00,000
-Riddikulus!   -Very good.

491
00:41:00,040 --> 00:41:02,730
A little louder and very clear. Listen,

492
00:41:02,740 --> 00:41:05,140
-Riddikulus!   -Riddikulus!

493
00:41:05,150 --> 00:41:07,440
-This class is ridiculous.   -Very good.

494
00:41:07,450 --> 00:41:11,430
So much for the easy part. You see, the incantation alone is not enough.

495
00:41:11,440 --> 00:41:15,370
What really finishes a boggart is laughter.

496
00:41:15,380 --> 00:41:19,940
You need to force it to assume a shape you find truly amusing.

497
00:41:19,950 --> 00:41:24,280
Let me explain. Neville, would you join me, please?

498
00:41:24,320 --> 00:41:26,820
Come on, don't be shy. Come on.

499
00:41:27,620 --> 00:41:29,520
Come on.

500
00:41:29,760 --> 00:41:33,450
Hello. Neville, what frightens you most of all?

501
00:41:33,460 --> 00:41:35,320
Professor Snape.

502
00:41:35,370 --> 00:41:37,360
-Sorry?   -Professor Snape.

503
00:41:37,370 --> 00:41:40,930
Professor Snape. Yes, frightens all.

504
00:41:40,940 --> 00:41:43,080
-You live with your grandmother.

505
00:41:43,090 --> 00:41:45,630
-I don't want it to turn into her, either.

506
00:41:45,940 --> 00:41:47,730
No...

507
00:41:48,380 --> 00:41:51,340
...it won't. I want you to picture her clothes.

508
00:41:51,410 --> 00:41:54,810
Only her clothes, very clearly, in your mind.

509
00:41:54,850 --> 00:41:58,080
-She carries a red handbag...   -We don't need to hear.

510
00:41:58,090 --> 00:41:59,940
As long as you see it, we'll see it.

511
00:41:59,950 --> 00:42:02,150
Now, when I open that wardrobe...

512
00:42:02,160 --> 00:42:05,660
...here's what I want you to do. Excuse me.

513
00:42:05,930 --> 00:42:09,060
Imagine Professor Snape in your grandmother's clothes.

514
00:42:09,060 --> 00:42:10,960
Can you do that?

515
00:42:11,370 --> 00:42:14,260
Yes. Wand at the ready.

516
00:42:14,400 --> 00:42:18,090
One, two, three.

517
00:42:27,680 --> 00:42:29,780
Think, Neville, think.

518
00:42:32,320 --> 00:42:34,580
Riddikulus!

519
00:42:38,930 --> 00:42:40,350
Wonderful, Neville, wonderful!

520
00:42:40,360 --> 00:42:41,790
Incredible! Okay...

521
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:44,900
...to the back, Neville. Everyone, form a line....

522
00:42:50,940 --> 00:42:52,430
Form a line!

523
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:56,040
I want everyone to picture the thing they fear the very most...

524
00:42:56,050 --> 00:42:59,340
...and turn it into something funny.

525
00:42:59,350 --> 00:43:01,240
Next! Ron!

526
00:43:04,290 --> 00:43:08,010
Concentrate. Face your fear. Be brave!

527
00:43:19,300 --> 00:43:21,020
Wand at the ready, Ron.

528
00:43:21,570 --> 00:43:23,560
Riddikulus!

529
00:43:23,570 --> 00:43:25,140
Yes!

530
00:43:25,540 --> 00:43:28,640
You see? Very good, very good!

531
00:43:28,940 --> 00:43:32,600
-Marvelous! Absolutely, very, very enjoyable!

532
00:43:32,610 --> 00:43:34,940
-Parvati! Next!

533
00:43:36,550 --> 00:43:38,950
Show us what you see.

534
00:43:48,030 --> 00:43:51,590
Keep your nerve. Steady.

535
00:43:51,600 --> 00:43:53,770
Riddikulus!

536
00:43:54,600 --> 00:43:56,770
And next! Step up, step up!

537
00:43:57,670 --> 00:43:59,700
Wonderful, wonderful!

538
00:44:13,520 --> 00:44:15,810
Here!

539
00:44:21,500 --> 00:44:23,490
Riddikulus!

540
00:44:31,810 --> 00:44:34,900
Right. Sorry about that. That's enough for today.

541
00:44:34,910 --> 00:44:37,070
Collect your books from the back.

542
00:44:37,080 --> 00:44:39,870
That's the end of the lesson. Thank you! Sorry!

543
00:44:39,880 --> 00:44:43,110
Sorry, you can have too much of a good thing.

544
00:44:44,920 --> 00:44:49,710
Remember, these visits to Hogsmeade village are a privilege.

545
00:44:49,790 --> 00:44:52,780
Should your behavior reflect poorly on the school...

546
00:44:52,790 --> 00:44:55,930
...that privilege shall not be extended again.

547
00:44:56,160 --> 00:44:57,580
No permission form signed,

548
00:44:57,590 --> 00:44:59,620
no visiting the village.

549
00:44:59,630 --> 00:45:01,360
That's the rule, Potter.

550
00:45:01,400 --> 00:45:02,790
Those with permission,

551
00:45:02,800 --> 00:45:04,760
follow me. Those without, stay put.

552
00:45:04,770 --> 00:45:07,430
I thought if you signed it, then I could...

553
00:45:07,440 --> 00:45:10,100
I can't. Only a parent or a guardian can sign.

554
00:45:10,110 --> 00:45:13,510
Since I am neither, it would be inappropriate.

555
00:45:15,620 --> 00:45:20,380
I'm sorry, Potter. That's my final word.

556
00:45:21,420 --> 00:45:24,850
Forget about it, guys. See you later.

557
00:45:38,470 --> 00:45:40,700
Professor, can I ask you something?

558
00:45:40,710 --> 00:45:44,770
You want to know why I stopped you facing that boggart, yes?

559
00:45:44,780 --> 00:45:46,340
I thought it'd be obvious.

560
00:45:46,350 --> 00:45:49,340
I assumed it would take the shape of Lord Voldemort.

561
00:45:49,350 --> 00:45:53,040
I did think of Voldemort at first.

562
00:45:53,090 --> 00:45:55,850
But then I remembered that night on the train...

563
00:45:55,860 --> 00:45:58,580
-...and the dementor.   -I'm very impressed.

564
00:45:58,590 --> 00:46:01,620
That suggests what you fear the most is fear itself.

565
00:46:01,630 --> 00:46:03,290
This is very wise.

566
00:46:03,300 --> 00:46:05,550
Before I fainted...

567
00:46:05,630 --> 00:46:07,820
...I heard something.

568
00:46:08,170 --> 00:46:09,990
A woman...

569
00:46:10,240 --> 00:46:11,800
...screaming.

570
00:46:11,810 --> 00:46:15,240
Dementors force us to relive our very worst memories.

571
00:46:15,240 --> 00:46:18,380
Our pain becomes their power.

572
00:46:19,010 --> 00:46:21,370
I think it was my mother...

573
00:46:21,380 --> 00:46:23,810
...the night she was murdered.

574
00:46:25,220 --> 00:46:27,730
The very first time I saw you, Harry,

575
00:46:27,740 --> 00:46:29,880
I recognized you immediately.

576
00:46:30,260 --> 00:46:33,320
Not by your scar, by your eyes.

577
00:46:33,530 --> 00:46:35,890
They're your mother, Lily's.

578
00:46:36,630 --> 00:46:38,260
Yes.

579
00:46:38,400 --> 00:46:41,590
Oh, yes. I knew her.

580
00:46:43,740 --> 00:46:47,770
Your mother was there for me at a time when no one else was.

581
00:46:47,770 --> 00:46:51,170
Not only was she a singularly gifted witch...

582
00:46:51,180 --> 00:46:54,710
...she was also an uncommonly kind woman.

583
00:46:55,020 --> 00:46:58,240
She had a way of seeing the beauty in others...

584
00:46:58,250 --> 00:47:04,620
...even, and most especially, when that person could not see it in themselves.

585
00:47:05,890 --> 00:47:08,750
And your father, James, on the other hand...

586
00:47:08,760 --> 00:47:10,490
...he....

587
00:47:10,800 --> 00:47:11,770
He had a certain,

588
00:47:11,780 --> 00:47:14,360
shall we say, talent for trouble.

589
00:47:16,440 --> 00:47:22,130
A talent, rumor has it, he passed on to you.

590
00:47:25,950 --> 00:47:29,110
You're more like them than you know, Harry.

591
00:47:29,750 --> 00:47:33,080
In time, you'll come to see just how much.

592
00:47:36,320 --> 00:47:38,240
Honeyduke's Sweetshop is brilliant,

593
00:47:38,250 --> 00:47:40,920
but nothing beats Zonko's Joke Shop.

594
00:47:40,930 --> 00:47:43,620
We never got to go to the Shrieking Shack.

595
00:47:43,630 --> 00:47:45,500
-You heard it's the most...

596
00:47:45,510 --> 00:47:47,890
-Haunted building in Britain. I know.

597
00:47:49,070 --> 00:47:50,730
What's going on?

598
00:47:50,740 --> 00:47:53,330
Probably Neville forgot the password again.

599
00:47:53,340 --> 00:47:55,930
-Hey.   -Oh, you're there.

600
00:47:55,940 --> 00:48:00,440
Let me through, please. Excuse me! I'm Head Boy!

601
00:48:01,850 --> 00:48:03,710
Get back, all of you.

602
00:48:03,720 --> 00:48:07,010
No one is to enter this dormitory until it's been searched.

603
00:48:07,020 --> 00:48:08,550
The Fat Lady! She's gone!

604
00:48:10,460 --> 00:48:13,080
Serves her right. She was a terrible singer.

605
00:48:13,090 --> 00:48:15,190
It's not funny, Ron.

606
00:48:17,000 --> 00:48:21,290
Keep calm, everyone. Break into fours. Back to your common room.

607
00:48:27,440 --> 00:48:28,600
-Be quiet.   -Make way.

608
00:48:28,610 --> 00:48:30,830
-The headmaster's here.   -Come on, move.

609
00:48:30,840 --> 00:48:32,940
You heard. Move!

610
00:48:46,960 --> 00:48:50,030
Mr. Filch? Round up the ghosts.

611
00:48:50,160 --> 00:48:54,460
Tell them to search every painting in the castle to find the Fat Lady.

612
00:48:54,470 --> 00:48:57,730
There's no need for ghosts, professor.

613
00:48:58,370 --> 00:49:00,700
The Fat Lady's there.

614
00:49:01,340 --> 00:49:03,530
Mind where you're going! Slow down!

615
00:49:03,910 --> 00:49:06,770
You listen! I'm Head Boy!

616
00:49:06,780 --> 00:49:09,380
-Come back here!   -Keep moving!

617
00:49:12,780 --> 00:49:15,850
Dear lady, who did this to you?

618
00:49:17,560 --> 00:49:19,750
Eyes like the devil,

619
00:49:19,760 --> 00:49:22,780
he's got, and a soul as dark as his name.

620
00:49:23,530 --> 00:49:26,690
It's him, headmaster. The one they all talk about.

621
00:49:26,700 --> 00:49:29,370
He's here, somewhere in the castle!

622
00:49:29,400 --> 00:49:31,760
Sirius Black!

623
00:49:31,800 --> 00:49:37,100
Secure the castle, Mr. Filch. The rest of you, to the Great Hall.

624
00:50:04,970 --> 00:50:10,060
I've searched the Astronomy Tower and the Owlery. There's nothing there.

625
00:50:10,070 --> 00:50:12,830
-Thank you.   -The third floor's clear too, sir.

626
00:50:12,840 --> 00:50:14,940
-Very good.   -I've done the dungeons.

627
00:50:14,950 --> 00:50:17,810
No sign of Black, nor anywhere else in the castle.

628
00:50:17,850 --> 00:50:20,540
I didn't really expect him to linger.

629
00:50:21,590 --> 00:50:24,080
Remarkable feat, don't you think?

630
00:50:24,090 --> 00:50:26,550
To enter Hogwarts Castle on one's own...

631
00:50:26,560 --> 00:50:29,420
-...completely undetected?   -Quite remarkable, yes.

632
00:50:29,430 --> 00:50:31,460
Any theories on how he managed it?

633
00:50:31,460 --> 00:50:34,630
Many. Each as unlikely as the next.

634
00:50:34,670 --> 00:50:36,390
You may recall...

635
00:50:36,400 --> 00:50:39,390
...prior to the start of term I expressed concerns...

636
00:50:39,400 --> 00:50:41,630
...about your appointment of Professor...

637
00:50:41,640 --> 00:50:45,900
Not a single professor inside this castle would help Sirius Black enter it.

638
00:50:45,910 --> 00:50:48,470
I'm quite convinced the castle is safe...

639
00:50:48,480 --> 00:50:52,270
...and I'm more than willing to send the students to their houses.

640
00:50:52,280 --> 00:50:54,810
What about Potter? Should he be warned?

641
00:50:54,820 --> 00:50:57,650
Perhaps. But for now, let him sleep.

642
00:50:58,320 --> 00:50:59,480
For in dreams,

643
00:50:59,490 --> 00:51:03,220
we enter a world that's entirely our own.

644
00:51:03,330 --> 00:51:10,020
Let them swim in the deepest ocean or glide over the highest cloud.

645
00:51:47,170 --> 00:51:50,700
Turn to page 394.

646
00:51:59,950 --> 00:52:03,710
Excuse me, sir. Where's Professor Lupin?

647
00:52:04,220 --> 00:52:07,810
That's not really your concern, is it, Potter?

648
00:52:07,820 --> 00:52:09,040
Suffice it to say

649
00:52:09,050 --> 00:52:11,890
your professor finds himself incapable of teaching...

650
00:52:11,900 --> 00:52:17,160
...at the present time. Turn to page 394.

651
00:52:21,770 --> 00:52:23,670
"Werewolves"?

652
00:52:23,770 --> 00:52:26,740
Sir, we just learned about red caps and hinkypunks.

653
00:52:26,780 --> 00:52:30,100
-We're not meant to start that for weeks.   -Quiet.

654
00:52:30,110 --> 00:52:33,480
When did she come in? Did you see her come in?

655
00:52:33,920 --> 00:52:37,610
Now, which one of you can tell me the difference...

656
00:52:37,620 --> 00:52:40,250
...between an Animagus and a werewolf?

657
00:52:40,760 --> 00:52:42,890
No one?

658
00:52:43,190 --> 00:52:46,290
-How disappointing.   -Please, sir.

659
00:52:46,300 --> 00:52:47,730
An Animagus is a wizard

660
00:52:47,740 --> 00:52:49,620
who elects to turn into an animal.

661
00:52:49,630 --> 00:52:51,390
A werewolf has no choice.

662
00:52:51,600 --> 00:52:53,490
With each full moon...

663
00:52:53,500 --> 00:52:57,570
...he no longer remembers who he is. He'd kill his best friend.

664
00:52:57,570 --> 00:53:01,330
The werewolf only responds to the call of its own kind.

665
00:53:02,310 --> 00:53:05,240
Thank you, Mr. Malfoy.

666
00:53:05,250 --> 00:53:07,740
That's the second time you've spoken out of turn, Miss Granger.

667
00:53:07,750 --> 00:53:09,910
Are you incapable of restraining yourself...

668
00:53:09,920 --> 00:53:13,450
...or do you take pride in being an insufferable know-it-all?

669
00:53:13,560 --> 00:53:17,160
-He's got a point, you know.   -Five points from Gryffindor.

670
00:53:17,160 --> 00:53:20,270
As an antidote to your ignorance, and on my desk,

671
00:53:20,280 --> 00:53:21,950
by Monday morning...

672
00:53:21,960 --> 00:53:24,680
...two rolls of parchment on the werewolf,

673
00:53:24,690 --> 00:53:25,830
with emphasis...

674
00:53:25,840 --> 00:53:27,180
-...on recognizing it.

675
00:53:27,190 --> 00:53:28,630
-It's Quidditch tomorrow.

676
00:53:29,540 --> 00:53:33,040
Then I suggest you take extra care, Mr. Potter.

677
00:53:33,080 --> 00:53:37,300
Loss of limb will not excuse you.

678
00:53:37,310 --> 00:53:41,280
Page 394.

679
00:53:43,090 --> 00:53:44,750
The term "werewolf"...

680
00:53:45,450 --> 00:53:50,150
...is a contraction of the Anglo-Saxon word " wer"...

681
00:53:50,690 --> 00:53:55,330
...which means "man," and "wolf." Werewolf, man-wolf.

682
00:53:55,800 --> 00:53:58,330
There are several ways to become a werewolf.

683
00:53:58,330 --> 00:54:01,530
They include being given the power of shape-shifting...

684
00:54:01,600 --> 00:54:03,700
...being bitten by a werewolf....

685
00:54:22,320 --> 00:54:26,150
Go, Harry! Go, Harry!

686
00:56:25,750 --> 00:56:28,780
Aresto momentum!

687
00:56:30,820 --> 00:56:34,110
-He looks a bit peaky, doesn't he?   -Peaky?

688
00:56:34,120 --> 00:56:36,580
What do you expect? He fell over 1 00 feet.

689
00:56:36,590 --> 00:56:38,300
Let's walk you off a tower

690
00:56:38,310 --> 00:56:39,660
and see what you look like.

691
00:56:39,660 --> 00:56:42,920
Probably a right sight better than he normally does.

692
00:56:46,370 --> 00:56:49,530
-How are you feeling?   -Oh, brilliant.

693
00:56:49,540 --> 00:56:51,700
You gave us a right good scare.

694
00:56:51,770 --> 00:56:52,770
-What happened?

695
00:56:52,780 --> 00:56:55,460
-Well, you fell off your broom.

696
00:56:55,540 --> 00:56:58,070
Really? I meant the match. Who won?

697
00:57:02,320 --> 00:57:04,210
No one blames you, Harry.

698
00:57:04,550 --> 00:57:08,550
Dementors aren't supposed to be on the grounds. Dumbledore's furious.

699
00:57:08,590 --> 00:57:10,810
After he saved you, he sent them off.

700
00:57:10,820 --> 00:57:14,690
There's something else you should know too.

701
00:57:15,060 --> 00:57:21,560
When you fell, your broom sort of blew into the Whomping Willow, and....

702
00:57:21,870 --> 00:57:23,560
Well....

703
00:57:24,640 --> 00:57:27,130
I'm sorry to hear about your broomstick.

704
00:57:27,240 --> 00:57:30,070
Is there no chance of fixing it?

705
00:57:30,080 --> 00:57:31,600
No.

706
00:57:31,610 --> 00:57:35,140
Professor, why do the dementors affect me so?

707
00:57:35,350 --> 00:57:38,610
-I mean, more than everyone else?   -Listen.

708
00:57:38,620 --> 00:57:41,980
Dementors are the foulest creatures to walk this earth.

709
00:57:41,990 --> 00:57:46,420
They feed on every good feeling, every happy memory...

710
00:57:46,790 --> 00:57:51,550
...until a person is left with absolutely nothing but his worst experiences.

711
00:57:51,600 --> 00:57:55,960
You are not weak, Harry.

712
00:57:55,970 --> 00:57:57,580
Dementors affect you most because

713
00:57:57,590 --> 00:58:00,230
there are true horrors in your past.

714
00:58:00,240 --> 00:58:03,530
Horrors your classmates can scarcely imagine.

715
00:58:03,810 --> 00:58:06,310
You have nothing to be ashamed of.

716
00:58:06,310 --> 00:58:08,160
-I'm scared, professor.

717
00:58:08,170 --> 00:58:10,510
-I'd consider you a fool if you weren't.

718
00:58:10,520 --> 00:58:14,180
I need to know how to fight them. You could teach me.

719
00:58:14,190 --> 00:58:16,380
You made the one on the train go away.

720
00:58:16,390 --> 00:58:18,350
There was only one that night.

721
00:58:18,430 --> 00:58:20,440
-But you made it go away.

722
00:58:20,450 --> 00:58:23,220
-I don't pretend to be an expert, Harry.

723
00:58:23,360 --> 00:58:28,490
But as the dementors seem to have developed an interest in you...

724
00:58:28,500 --> 00:58:32,330
...perhaps I should teach you. But after the holidays.

725
00:58:32,340 --> 00:58:34,440
For now, I need to rest.

726
00:58:59,700 --> 00:59:04,160
Last call for Hogsmeade! Come on, now!

727
00:59:19,590 --> 00:59:21,740
-Guys, let me go.   -Clever, Harry.

728
00:59:21,750 --> 00:59:24,810
-But not clever enough.   -We've got a better way.

729
00:59:24,820 --> 00:59:27,820
-I'm trying to get to Hogsmeade.   -We know.

730
00:59:27,830 --> 00:59:29,350
We'll get you there.

731
00:59:29,360 --> 00:59:30,840
-We'll show you a quicker way.

732
00:59:30,850 --> 00:59:32,090
-lf you pipe down.

733
00:59:32,100 --> 00:59:33,080
-Bless him.

734
00:59:33,090 --> 00:59:35,890
-Let me go! Come on, guys. Don't...

735
00:59:36,300 --> 00:59:39,090
-Now, Harry.   -Come and join the big boys.

736
00:59:40,310 --> 00:59:42,630
What are you doing?!

737
00:59:42,710 --> 00:59:43,900
-What's this rubbish?

738
00:59:43,910 --> 00:59:45,710
-"What's this rubbish?" he says.

739
00:59:45,710 --> 00:59:47,270
-It's the secret to our success.

740
00:59:47,280 --> 00:59:49,210
-It's a wrench giving it to you...

741
00:59:49,210 --> 00:59:52,270
But we've decided your needs are greater than ours.

742
00:59:52,280 --> 00:59:54,210
George, if you will.

743
00:59:54,220 --> 00:59:57,680
I solemnly swear that I am up to no good.

744
01:00:01,130 --> 01:00:04,920
" Messrs. Moony, Wormtail, Padfoot and Prongs...

745
01:00:05,130 --> 01:00:08,300
...are proud to present the Marauder's Map."

746
01:00:08,330 --> 01:00:10,800
We owe them so much.

747
01:00:14,140 --> 01:00:18,130
Hang on. This is Hogwarts. And that...

748
01:00:18,140 --> 01:00:21,040
-No. Is that really...?   -Dumbledore.

749
01:00:21,050 --> 01:00:22,200
-ln his study.   -Pacing.

750
01:00:22,210 --> 01:00:24,440
Does that a lot.

751
01:00:24,450 --> 01:00:26,480
-So this map shows...?   -Everyone.

752
01:00:26,480 --> 01:00:28,640
-Where they are.   -What they're doing.

753
01:00:28,650 --> 01:00:29,940
-Every minute.   -Every day.

754
01:00:29,950 --> 01:00:31,860
-Brilliant! Where did you get it?

755
01:00:31,870 --> 01:00:33,110
-From Filch's office.

756
01:00:33,120 --> 01:00:36,020
-First year.   -There are seven secret passageways...

757
01:00:36,030 --> 01:00:38,850
-...out of the castle.   -We'd recommend this one.

758
01:00:38,860 --> 01:00:42,190
-The One-Eyed Witch passageway.   -Leads you to Honeyduke's.

759
01:00:42,200 --> 01:00:44,190
Hurry. Filch is heading this way.

760
01:00:44,200 --> 01:00:47,800
And don't forget. When you're done, just give it a tap and say:

761
01:00:47,810 --> 01:00:52,340
"Mischief managed." Otherwise, anyone can read it.0

762
01:01:27,450 --> 01:01:29,870
Now, how much do you want?

763
01:01:36,950 --> 01:01:39,090
Delicious.

764
01:01:46,900 --> 01:01:51,130
It's meant to be the most haunted building in Britain. Did I mention that?

765
01:01:51,140 --> 01:01:53,030
Twice.

766
01:01:53,540 --> 01:01:56,070
Do you want to move a bit closer?

767
01:01:56,070 --> 01:01:57,970
To the Shrieking Shack?

768
01:01:58,080 --> 01:02:01,100
Actually, I'm fine here.

769
01:02:01,110 --> 01:02:03,140
Well, well. Look who's here.

770
01:02:03,350 --> 01:02:05,810
You two shopping for your new dream home?

771
01:02:05,850 --> 01:02:08,110
Bit grand for you, isn't it, Weasle-Bee?

772
01:02:08,120 --> 01:02:10,320
Don't your family sleep in one room?

773
01:02:10,350 --> 01:02:13,750
-Shut your mouth, Malfoy.   -Not very friendly.

774
01:02:13,860 --> 01:02:16,940
Boys, I think it's time we teach Weasle-Bee...

775
01:02:16,950 --> 01:02:19,150
...how to respect his superiors.

776
01:02:19,160 --> 01:02:20,930
-Hope you don't mean yourself.

777
01:02:20,940 --> 01:02:22,760
-How dare you talk to me!

778
01:02:22,770 --> 01:02:24,960
You filthy little mudblood!

779
01:02:28,970 --> 01:02:30,700
Who is that?

780
01:02:36,750 --> 01:02:39,310
-Don't stand there! Do something!   -What?

781
01:02:58,940 --> 01:03:01,400
What's up, Malfoy? Lost your skis?

782
01:03:05,180 --> 01:03:06,810
Get out of the way!

783
01:03:07,080 --> 01:03:08,840
Move!

784
01:03:08,850 --> 01:03:12,040
Malfoy! Wait! Wait!

785
01:03:15,620 --> 01:03:17,710
Harry!

786
01:03:17,720 --> 01:03:21,980
-Bloody hell, Harry.   -That was not funny.

787
01:03:22,960 --> 01:03:26,390
Those weasels! Never told me about any Marauder's Map.

788
01:03:26,430 --> 01:03:30,030
He won't keep it. He'll turn it over to Professor McGonagall.

789
01:03:30,070 --> 01:03:34,190
-Aren't you?   -Sure. Along with his lnvisibility Cloak.

790
01:03:34,200 --> 01:03:36,890
Look who it is. Madam Rosmerta.

791
01:03:36,940 --> 01:03:39,370
-Ron fancies her.   -That's not true!

792
01:03:39,380 --> 01:03:41,440
-Professor McGonagall!   -Cornelius!

793
01:03:41,440 --> 01:03:43,010
Allow me, minister.

794
01:03:43,010 --> 01:03:45,040
-Oh, Hagrid....   -Sorry about that.

795
01:03:45,050 --> 01:03:48,180
Rosmerta, my dear. I hope business is good.

796
01:03:48,180 --> 01:03:52,210
It'd be a lot better if the Ministry wasn't sending dementors...

797
01:03:52,220 --> 01:03:54,560
-...into my pub every other night!

798
01:03:54,570 --> 01:03:56,450
-We have....

799
01:03:56,690 --> 01:03:58,330
-We have a killer on the loose.

800
01:03:58,340 --> 01:04:00,090
-Sirius Black in Hogsmeade!

801
01:04:00,230 --> 01:04:02,820
And what would bring him here?

802
01:04:02,830 --> 01:04:07,160
-Harry Potter.   -Harry Potter?

803
01:04:07,170 --> 01:04:09,130
Come.

804
01:04:11,480 --> 01:04:13,670
Harry!

805
01:04:21,190 --> 01:04:23,850
-No underage wizards allowed in today!

806
01:04:23,860 --> 01:04:25,840
-Shut the damn door!

807
01:04:25,860 --> 01:04:28,050
-So rude.   -Thick heads.

808
01:04:28,090 --> 01:04:29,880
-Thick heads?!   -How dare they!

809
01:04:29,890 --> 01:04:33,260
-Who are they calling thick heads?   -Young whippersnappers!

810
01:04:33,830 --> 01:04:37,890
Nobody will come to a pub where they'll get scared out of their wits.

811
01:04:37,900 --> 01:04:42,040
Professor Dumbledore doesn't want dementors around the place.

812
01:04:44,610 --> 01:04:46,570
Tell me what this is all about.

813
01:04:46,580 --> 01:04:47,280
Years ago,

814
01:04:47,290 --> 01:04:51,210
when Harry Potter's parents realized they were marked for death...

815
01:04:51,220 --> 01:04:54,080
Remember? They hid. Few knew where they were.

816
01:04:54,090 --> 01:04:56,220
One who did was Sirius Black.

817
01:04:56,230 --> 01:04:58,120
And he told You-Know-Who.

818
01:04:58,120 --> 01:05:01,520
Not only did Black lead him to the Potters that night...

819
01:05:01,530 --> 01:05:05,090
...he also killed Peter Pettigrew!

820
01:05:05,130 --> 01:05:07,490
-Peter Pettigrew?   -Little lump of a boy.

821
01:05:07,500 --> 01:05:09,890
-Always trailing after Black.   -I remember.

822
01:05:09,900 --> 01:05:11,890
Never let James and Sirius out of his sight.

823
01:05:11,900 --> 01:05:12,870
-What happened?

824
01:05:12,880 --> 01:05:14,800
-Peter tried to warn the Potters...

825
01:05:14,810 --> 01:05:16,470
...and might have,

826
01:05:16,480 --> 01:05:19,200
had he not run into an old friend, Sirius Black.

827
01:05:19,210 --> 01:05:23,240
Black was vicious. He didn't kill Pettigrew.

828
01:05:23,250 --> 01:05:25,610
He destroyed him!

829
01:05:26,050 --> 01:05:28,580
A finger. That's all that was left.

830
01:05:28,590 --> 01:05:30,950
A finger. Nothing else.

831
01:05:30,960 --> 01:05:34,150
Sirius Black may not have put his hands to the Potters...

832
01:05:34,160 --> 01:05:36,080
-...but he's the reason they're dead.

833
01:05:36,090 --> 01:05:37,590
-He wants to finish things.

834
01:05:37,600 --> 01:05:40,630
-I don't believe it.   -That's not the worst of it.

835
01:05:40,630 --> 01:05:42,290
-What could be worse?

836
01:05:42,300 --> 01:05:44,600
-This: Sirius Black was...

837
01:05:44,600 --> 01:05:46,930
...and remains to this day...

838
01:05:47,170 --> 01:05:49,000
...Harry Potter's godfather!

839
01:05:57,450 --> 01:05:59,940
Ron, look!

840
01:06:05,460 --> 01:06:08,250
-Sorry. Excuse me, excuse me.   -Merry Christmas.

841
01:06:46,500 --> 01:06:48,530
Harry, what happened?

842
01:06:50,840 --> 01:06:53,160
He was their friend...

843
01:06:53,470 --> 01:06:55,900
...and he betrayed them.

844
01:06:56,510 --> 01:06:58,670
He was their friend!

845
01:07:00,710 --> 01:07:02,880
I hope he finds me.

846
01:07:03,310 --> 01:07:05,850
Because when he does, I'm gonna be ready!

847
01:07:06,120 --> 01:07:08,910
When he does, I'm gonna kill him!

848
01:07:23,000 --> 01:07:24,830
Harry.

849
01:07:25,140 --> 01:07:26,960
There you are. You came.

850
01:07:27,170 --> 01:07:29,240
Are you sure about this, Harry?

851
01:07:29,250 --> 01:07:31,200
This is very advanced magic...

852
01:07:31,210 --> 01:07:33,830
...well beyond the Ordinary Wizarding Level.

853
01:07:33,840 --> 01:07:35,570
I'm sure.

854
01:07:35,950 --> 01:07:38,610
Well, everything's prepared.

855
01:07:38,680 --> 01:07:42,250
The spell I'm going to teach you is called the Patronus Charm.

856
01:07:42,250 --> 01:07:43,880
Did you ever hear of it?

857
01:07:43,890 --> 01:07:45,710
No? Well....

858
01:07:45,720 --> 01:07:47,350
A Patronus is a positive force.

859
01:07:47,360 --> 01:07:49,450
For the wizard who conjures one...

860
01:07:49,460 --> 01:07:51,420
...it works like a shield,

861
01:07:51,430 --> 01:07:54,290
with the dementor feeding on it rather than him.

862
01:07:54,300 --> 01:07:58,290
But in order for it to work, you need to think of a memory.

863
01:07:58,300 --> 01:07:59,610
Not just any memory,

864
01:07:59,620 --> 01:08:02,460
a very happy memory, a very powerful memory.

865
01:08:02,470 --> 01:08:06,470
Can you do this? Yes. Very well.

866
01:08:07,480 --> 01:08:09,910
Close your eyes.

867
01:08:11,480 --> 01:08:13,580
Concentrate.

868
01:08:14,620 --> 01:08:16,910
Explore your past.

869
01:08:17,220 --> 01:08:19,280
Do you have a memory?

870
01:08:20,690 --> 01:08:23,080
Allow it to fill you up.

871
01:08:23,590 --> 01:08:25,890
Lose yourself within it.

872
01:08:26,000 --> 01:08:31,530
Then speak the incantation, Expecto Patronum.

873
01:08:31,770 --> 01:08:34,800
-Expecto Patronum.   -Very good.

874
01:08:38,410 --> 01:08:41,940
Shall we? Wand at the ready.

875
01:08:59,560 --> 01:09:02,360
Expecto Patronum!

876
01:09:02,930 --> 01:09:06,500
Expecto.... Expecto....

877
01:09:06,540 --> 01:09:08,460
Expect....

878
01:09:10,270 --> 01:09:14,530
Here we go. Come on. Sit up. Deep breaths.

879
01:09:14,640 --> 01:09:18,640
It's all right. I didn't expect you to do it the first time.

880
01:09:18,850 --> 01:09:21,010
That would have been remarkable.

881
01:09:21,020 --> 01:09:24,180
Here, eat this. You'll feel better.

882
01:09:24,820 --> 01:09:27,890
-That's one nasty dementor.   -Oh, no, no, no.

883
01:09:27,890 --> 01:09:30,820
That was a boggart, Harry. A boggart.

884
01:09:30,830 --> 01:09:34,150
The real thing would be worse. Much, much worse.

885
01:09:34,160 --> 01:09:36,960
As a matter of interest, what were you thinking?

886
01:09:36,970 --> 01:09:40,860
-Which memory did you choose?   -The first time I rode a broom.

887
01:09:41,870 --> 01:09:45,400
That's not good enough. Not nearly good enough.

888
01:09:52,080 --> 01:09:57,550
There's another. It's not happy, exactly.

889
01:09:59,290 --> 01:10:01,550
Well, it is.

890
01:10:01,560 --> 01:10:04,320
It's the happiest I've ever felt...

891
01:10:04,330 --> 01:10:08,490
-...but it's complicated.   -ls it strong?

892
01:10:12,670 --> 01:10:15,700
Then let's give it a try. You feel ready?

893
01:10:17,310 --> 01:10:19,240
Just do it.

894
01:10:29,080 --> 01:10:32,550
Expecto Patronum!

895
01:10:33,590 --> 01:10:37,750
Expecto Patronum!

896
01:10:59,150 --> 01:11:00,440
Yes!

897
01:11:02,220 --> 01:11:05,820
Well done, Harry. Well done!

898
01:11:06,160 --> 01:11:07,960
-I think I've had enough for today.

899
01:11:07,970 --> 01:11:10,450
-Yes. Sit down. Here.

900
01:11:10,460 --> 01:11:13,050
Eat this, it helps. It really helps.

901
01:11:13,060 --> 01:11:14,990
And just so you know, Harry...

902
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:19,160
...I think you'd have given your father a run for his money. And that...

903
01:11:19,170 --> 01:11:21,430
...is saying something.

904
01:11:23,410 --> 01:11:25,570
I was thinking of him.

905
01:11:25,580 --> 01:11:27,900
And Mum.

906
01:11:27,910 --> 01:11:30,340
Seeing their faces.

907
01:11:30,780 --> 01:11:33,640
They were talking to me.

908
01:11:33,650 --> 01:11:36,080
Just talking.

909
01:11:36,090 --> 01:11:38,620
That's the memory I chose.

910
01:11:40,020 --> 01:11:42,690
I don't even know if it's real.

911
01:11:42,990 --> 01:11:45,350
But it's the best I have.

912
01:11:54,400 --> 01:11:56,900
-Beautiful day.   -Gorgeous.

913
01:11:56,910 --> 01:11:59,030
Unless you've been ripped to pieces!

914
01:11:59,040 --> 01:12:01,630
Ripped to pieces? What are you talking about?

915
01:12:01,640 --> 01:12:04,970
-Ronald has lost his rat.   -I haven't lost anything!

916
01:12:04,980 --> 01:12:07,270
-Your cat killed him!   -Rubbish.

917
01:12:07,280 --> 01:12:10,780
Harry, you've seen the way that bloodthirsty beast of hers...

918
01:12:10,790 --> 01:12:13,050
...is always lurking about.

919
01:12:13,060 --> 01:12:14,850
And Scabbers is gone.

920
01:12:14,860 --> 01:12:17,920
Well, maybe you should take better care of your pets!

921
01:12:17,930 --> 01:12:20,150
-Your cat killed him!   -Did not.

922
01:12:20,160 --> 01:12:21,850
-Did.   -Didn't.

923
01:12:23,700 --> 01:12:26,490
How did it go, Hagrid? The hearing?

924
01:12:26,500 --> 01:12:29,960
Well, first off, the committee members took turns...

925
01:12:29,970 --> 01:12:32,830
...talking about why we were there.

926
01:12:34,510 --> 01:12:37,340
I got up and did my piece. Said how Buckbeak...

927
01:12:37,350 --> 01:12:39,130
...was a good hippogriff,

928
01:12:39,140 --> 01:12:40,510
always cleaned his feathers.

929
01:12:40,520 --> 01:12:42,770
And then Lucius Malfoy got up. Well,

930
01:12:42,780 --> 01:12:43,710
you can imagine.

931
01:12:43,720 --> 01:12:47,080
He said Buckbeak was a deadly and dangerous creature...

932
01:12:47,090 --> 01:12:50,350
...who would kill you as soon as look at you.

933
01:12:50,360 --> 01:12:52,360
And then?

934
01:12:52,860 --> 01:12:55,720
And then he asked for the worst, did old Lucius.

935
01:12:55,730 --> 01:13:00,060
-They're not sacking you!   -No, I'm not sacked.

936
01:13:01,970 --> 01:13:05,160
Buckbeak's been sentenced to death!

937
01:13:31,830 --> 01:13:35,180
Spiders! There's... There's spiders. Spiders.

938
01:13:35,190 --> 01:13:37,560
They want me to tap-dance.

939
01:13:37,570 --> 01:13:40,300
-I don't wanna tap-dance!   -You tell those spiders.

940
01:13:40,310 --> 01:13:44,470
Right, yeah. Tell them. I'll tell them....

941
01:14:02,430 --> 01:14:04,760
-Peter Pettigrew/   -Little lump of a boy.

942
01:14:04,770 --> 01:14:08,090
-Always trailing after Sirius Black.   -Black was vicious.

943
01:14:08,100 --> 01:14:10,770
He didn 't kill Pettigrew, he destroyed him!

944
01:14:18,650 --> 01:14:22,300
-Put that light out!   -Sorry.

945
01:15:05,360 --> 01:15:09,690
-Watch it there, boy.   -We're trying to sleep here!

946
01:15:17,710 --> 01:15:20,500
Mischief managed. Nox.

947
01:15:22,510 --> 01:15:24,000
Potter.

948
01:15:24,010 --> 01:15:27,670
What are you doing wandering the corridors at night?

949
01:15:27,680 --> 01:15:28,910
I was sleepwalking.

950
01:15:28,920 --> 01:15:31,710
How extraordinarily like your father you are, Potter.

951
01:15:31,720 --> 01:15:36,690
He, too, was exceedingly arrogant, strutting about the castle.

952
01:15:36,690 --> 01:15:41,220
My dad didn't strut. And nor do l.

953
01:15:41,760 --> 01:15:45,020
Now, if you don't mind, I would appreciate it if you could lower your wand.

954
01:15:48,380 --> 01:15:50,410
Turn out your pockets.

955
01:15:51,890 --> 01:15:54,710
Turn out your pockets!

956
01:15:57,430 --> 01:15:59,220
What's this?

957
01:15:59,230 --> 01:16:02,690
-Spare bit of parchment.   -Really? Open it.

958
01:16:09,070 --> 01:16:12,870
Reveal your secrets.

959
01:16:16,550 --> 01:16:18,210
Read it.

960
01:16:20,450 --> 01:16:26,140
" Messrs. Moony, Wormtail, Padfoot, and Prongs...

961
01:16:26,160 --> 01:16:30,450
...offer their compliments to Professor Snape and...."

962
01:16:30,560 --> 01:16:32,250
Go on.

963
01:16:33,230 --> 01:16:37,300
"And request he keep his large nose out of other people's business."

964
01:16:37,300 --> 01:16:40,060
-You insolent little...   -Professor!

965
01:16:41,470 --> 01:16:44,360
Well, well. Lupin.

966
01:16:44,370 --> 01:16:49,270
Out for a little walk in the moonlight, are we?

967
01:16:50,450 --> 01:16:53,080
Harry, are you all right?

968
01:16:53,080 --> 01:16:55,750
That remains to be seen.

969
01:16:56,380 --> 01:17:00,280
I have now just confiscated a rather curious artifact.

970
01:17:00,290 --> 01:17:03,980
Take a look, Lupin. Supposed to be your area of expertise.

971
01:17:03,990 --> 01:17:06,300
-Clearly, it's full of dark magic.

972
01:17:06,310 --> 01:17:08,950
-I seriously doubt it, Severus.

973
01:17:08,960 --> 01:17:12,620
It looks as though it's a parchment designed to insult anyone...

974
01:17:12,630 --> 01:17:16,700
...who tries to read it. I suspect it's a Zonko product.

975
01:17:16,710 --> 01:17:21,100
Nevertheless, I shall investigate any hidden qualities it may possess.

976
01:17:21,110 --> 01:17:24,400
It is, after all, as you say, my area of expertise.

977
01:17:24,410 --> 01:17:27,940
Harry, would you come with me, please? Professor, good night.

978
01:17:33,760 --> 01:17:36,680
Are you deaf? Put that light out!

979
01:17:41,600 --> 01:17:43,230
Come in.

980
01:17:44,830 --> 01:17:50,230
I haven't the faintest idea how this map came to be in your possession...

981
01:17:50,240 --> 01:17:54,870
...but quite frankly, I am astounded that you didn't hand it in.

982
01:17:54,880 --> 01:17:56,000
Did it never occur to you that this,

983
01:17:56,010 --> 01:17:58,740
in the hands of Sirius Black...

984
01:17:58,750 --> 01:18:00,940
...is a map to you?

985
01:18:01,550 --> 01:18:04,220
-No.   -No, sir.

986
01:18:06,020 --> 01:18:09,250
Your father never set much store by the rules either.

987
01:18:09,260 --> 01:18:13,760
But he and your mother gave their lives to save yours.

988
01:18:14,200 --> 01:18:16,230
Gambling their sacrifice

989
01:18:16,240 --> 01:18:18,460
by wandering the castle unprotected...

990
01:18:18,470 --> 01:18:20,470
...with a killer on the loose seems

991
01:18:20,480 --> 01:18:23,100
to me a poor way to repay them!

992
01:18:23,140 --> 01:18:25,460
Now, I will not cover up for you again.

993
01:18:25,470 --> 01:18:28,070
-Do you hear me?   -Yes, sir.

994
01:18:28,080 --> 01:18:31,900
I want you to return to your dormitory and stay there.

995
01:18:31,910 --> 01:18:34,280
And don't take any detours.

996
01:18:34,290 --> 01:18:36,880
If you do, I shall know.

997
01:18:41,360 --> 01:18:45,990
Professor, just so you know, I don't think that map always works.

998
01:18:46,660 --> 01:18:49,320
Earlier, it showed someone in the castle.

999
01:18:49,330 --> 01:18:51,800
Someone I know to be dead.

1000
01:18:52,030 --> 01:18:54,930
Oh, really? And who might that be?

1001
01:18:54,940 --> 01:18:56,690
Peter Pettigrew.

1002
01:18:59,110 --> 01:19:01,400
That's not possible.

1003
01:19:02,410 --> 01:19:04,270
It's just what I saw.

1004
01:19:06,920 --> 01:19:08,810
Good night, professor.

1005
01:19:12,120 --> 01:19:16,450
Broaden your minds. You must look beyond.

1006
01:19:16,460 --> 01:19:22,050
The art of crystal gazing is in the clearing of the lnner Eye.

1007
01:19:22,060 --> 01:19:25,600
Only then can you see. Try again.

1008
01:19:25,930 --> 01:19:28,230
Now, what do we have here?

1009
01:19:30,370 --> 01:19:32,770
Do you mind me trying?

1010
01:19:34,980 --> 01:19:38,140
The Grim, possibly.

1011
01:19:40,120 --> 01:19:44,380
My dear, from the first moment you stepped foot in my class...

1012
01:19:44,390 --> 01:19:48,350
...I sensed that you did not possess the proper spirit...

1013
01:19:48,360 --> 01:19:52,420
...for the noble art of Divination. No, you see, there.

1014
01:19:52,430 --> 01:19:56,250
You may be young in years, but your heart is as shriveled...

1015
01:19:56,260 --> 01:19:58,050
...as an old maid's,

1016
01:19:58,060 --> 01:20:00,430
your soul as dry as the pages of the books...

1017
01:20:00,440 --> 01:20:03,760
...to which you so desperately cleave.

1018
01:20:19,090 --> 01:20:21,280
Have I said something?

1019
01:20:25,760 --> 01:20:27,670
She's gone mental, Hermione has.

1020
01:20:27,680 --> 01:20:30,920
Not that she wasn't always mental...

1021
01:20:30,930 --> 01:20:33,660
...but now it's in the open for everyone to see.

1022
01:20:33,670 --> 01:20:36,030
Hang on.

1023
01:20:36,040 --> 01:20:39,140
-We better take this back.   -I'm not going back.

1024
01:20:39,270 --> 01:20:42,870
-Fine. See you later.   -See you.

1025
01:21:20,450 --> 01:21:25,910
Harry Potter....

1026
01:21:32,590 --> 01:21:37,020
-Professor Trelawney...   -He will return tonight.

1027
01:21:37,030 --> 01:21:38,860
Sorry?

1028
01:21:38,870 --> 01:21:40,870
Tonight, he who betrayed his friends,

1029
01:21:40,880 --> 01:21:43,660
whose heart rots with murder...

1030
01:21:43,670 --> 01:21:45,860
...shall break free.

1031
01:21:45,870 --> 01:21:48,270
Innocent blood shall be spilt...

1032
01:21:48,280 --> 01:21:54,470
...and servant and master shall be reunited once more.

1033
01:22:00,620 --> 01:22:04,090
I'm so sorry, dear boy. Did you say something?

1034
01:22:04,690 --> 01:22:06,690
No.

1035
01:22:06,930 --> 01:22:08,680
Nothing.

1036
01:23:01,080 --> 01:23:05,280
I can't believe they're going to kill Buckbeak. It's just too horrible.

1037
01:23:05,290 --> 01:23:08,180
-lt just got worse.   -What did I say? Father said...

1038
01:23:08,190 --> 01:23:10,780
...I can keep the hippogriff's head.

1039
01:23:10,790 --> 01:23:12,550
I'll donate it to the Gryffindors' room.

1040
01:23:12,560 --> 01:23:15,190
This is going to be rich.

1041
01:23:15,200 --> 01:23:17,560
-Look who's here.   -Come to see the show?

1042
01:23:17,560 --> 01:23:20,820
You! You foul, loathsome, evil little cockroach!

1043
01:23:20,830 --> 01:23:22,800
Hermione, no!

1044
01:23:23,170 --> 01:23:25,630
He's not worth it.

1045
01:23:39,520 --> 01:23:41,780
Malfoy, are you okay?

1046
01:23:41,790 --> 01:23:46,150
-Let's go. Quick.   -Not a word to anyone, understood?

1047
01:23:46,160 --> 01:23:50,800
-That felt good.   -Not good, brilliant.

1048
01:24:10,020 --> 01:24:14,480
Look at him. Loves the smell of the trees when the wind blows through them.

1049
01:24:14,490 --> 01:24:16,910
Why don't we just set him free?

1050
01:24:16,920 --> 01:24:19,520
They'd know it was me, and then Dumbledore...

1051
01:24:19,530 --> 01:24:22,690
...would get into trouble. He's coming down, Dumbledore.

1052
01:24:22,700 --> 01:24:25,260
Says he wants to be with me when they....

1053
01:24:26,070 --> 01:24:28,260
When it happens.

1054
01:24:28,270 --> 01:24:29,830
Great man, Dumbledore.

1055
01:24:30,640 --> 01:24:32,360
A great man.

1056
01:24:34,640 --> 01:24:36,180
-We'll stay with you too.

1057
01:24:36,190 --> 01:24:37,770
-You'll do no such thing!

1058
01:24:37,780 --> 01:24:41,140
Think I want you seeing something like that? No.

1059
01:24:41,150 --> 01:24:42,730
You just drink your tea and be off. Oh.

1060
01:24:42,740 --> 01:24:44,980
Before you do, Ron....

1061
01:24:52,230 --> 01:24:54,750
Scabbers! You're alive!

1062
01:24:54,760 --> 01:24:56,680
-Keep a closer eye on your pet.

1063
01:24:56,690 --> 01:24:58,660
-I think you owe someone an apology.

1064
01:24:58,660 --> 01:25:02,560
Right. Next time I see Crookshanks, I'll let him know.

1065
01:25:02,570 --> 01:25:03,860
I meant me!

1066
01:25:04,370 --> 01:25:06,760
Blimey. What was that?

1067
01:25:13,050 --> 01:25:14,640
Hagrid!

1068
01:25:16,380 --> 01:25:17,910
Oh, crikey.

1069
01:25:19,190 --> 01:25:22,110
No, minister. Over this way.

1070
01:25:22,120 --> 01:25:26,380
It's late. It's nearly dark. You shouldn't be here.

1071
01:25:26,390 --> 01:25:28,890
Someone sees you outside this time of night,

1072
01:25:28,900 --> 01:25:30,320
you'll be in trouble.

1073
01:25:30,330 --> 01:25:34,120
Particularly you, Harry. With you in a moment!

1074
01:25:35,330 --> 01:25:37,930
Quick. Quick!

1075
01:25:37,940 --> 01:25:39,830
Hagrid.

1076
01:25:39,840 --> 01:25:43,970
-lt'll be fine. It'll be okay.   -Go on, go on!

1077
01:25:45,610 --> 01:25:47,810
-That's ling you see over there...

1078
01:25:47,820 --> 01:25:48,570
-On the slope.

1079
01:25:48,580 --> 01:25:50,340
-On the slope... Ah, Hagrid.

1080
01:25:50,350 --> 01:25:51,410
-Professor Dumbledore.

1081
01:25:51,420 --> 01:25:54,310
-Good evening.   -Minister. Make your way through.

1082
01:25:54,320 --> 01:25:58,350
-Have a tea, if you like.   -No, Hagrid.

1083
01:26:00,260 --> 01:26:03,020
-Gentlemen.   -I'd like a cup of tea.

1084
01:26:03,030 --> 01:26:06,560
Well, I think we should get down to our business, shall we?

1085
01:26:07,530 --> 01:26:11,300
Very well. It is the decision of the Committee for the Disposal...

1086
01:26:11,310 --> 01:26:14,630
...of Dangerous Creatures that the hippogriff Buckbeak...

1087
01:26:14,640 --> 01:26:17,730
...hereinafter called "the condemned,"

1088
01:26:17,740 --> 01:26:20,300
shall be executed this day at sundown.

1089
01:26:20,310 --> 01:26:21,990
-Dear, dear....

1090
01:26:22,000 --> 01:26:24,040
-Now, now, Hagrid. Now, come on.

1091
01:26:24,050 --> 01:26:28,610
-All right. It'll be all right.   -The execution shall dispatch...

1092
01:26:28,620 --> 01:26:30,510
What?

1093
01:26:30,520 --> 01:26:32,780
I thought I just saw...

1094
01:26:32,790 --> 01:26:35,090
-Never mind.   -Let's go!

1095
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:42,530
Buckbeak didn't mean no harm.

1096
01:27:28,850 --> 01:27:30,510
Oh, no.

1097
01:27:41,230 --> 01:27:43,620
He bit me. Scabbers.

1098
01:27:44,030 --> 01:27:46,160
Ron. Ron!

1099
01:27:46,930 --> 01:27:50,660
-Ron!   -Scabbers, come back.

1100
01:27:51,970 --> 01:27:53,930
Wait!

1101
01:27:59,650 --> 01:28:01,700
-Scabbers, you bit me!

1102
01:28:01,710 --> 01:28:04,110
-Harry, you do realize what tree this is?

1103
01:28:04,120 --> 01:28:06,610
That's not good. Ron, run!

1104
01:28:09,560 --> 01:28:12,280
Harry, Hermione, run!

1105
01:28:12,660 --> 01:28:14,480
It's the Grim!

1106
01:28:21,300 --> 01:28:24,560
-Harry!   -Ron! Ron, wait!

1107
01:28:24,570 --> 01:28:26,760
Harry!

1108
01:28:28,140 --> 01:28:30,710
-Help!   -Ron!

1109
01:28:32,650 --> 01:28:36,110
-Ron. Ron.   -Ron!

1110
01:28:50,760 --> 01:28:52,950
Come on!

1111
01:28:54,670 --> 01:28:56,300
Move!

1112
01:29:00,140 --> 01:29:02,100
Duck!

1113
01:29:37,740 --> 01:29:40,240
Harry!

1114
01:29:55,960 --> 01:29:59,090
-Oh, I'm sorry.   -Don't worry.

1115
01:29:59,100 --> 01:30:03,230
-Where do you suppose this goes?   -I have a hunch.

1116
01:30:03,570 --> 01:30:05,260
I just hope I'm wrong.

1117
01:30:24,760 --> 01:30:28,120
We're in the Shrieking Shack, aren't we?

1118
01:30:29,030 --> 01:30:30,820
Come on.

1119
01:30:41,010 --> 01:30:42,600
Ron.

1120
01:30:42,940 --> 01:30:45,770
-Ron. You're okay.   -The dog. Where is it?

1121
01:30:45,780 --> 01:30:49,210
It's a trap. He's the dog. He's an Animagus.

1122
01:31:02,900 --> 01:31:05,820
If you want to kill Harry, you have to kill us too!

1123
01:31:05,830 --> 01:31:07,620
No. Only one will die tonight.

1124
01:31:07,630 --> 01:31:09,770
Then it'll be you!

1125
01:31:15,780 --> 01:31:18,140
Are you going to kill me, Harry?

1126
01:31:19,150 --> 01:31:21,180
Expelliarmus!

1127
01:31:24,720 --> 01:31:29,080
Well, well, Sirius. Looking rather ragged, aren't we?

1128
01:31:29,090 --> 01:31:32,310
Finally, the flesh reflects the madness within.

1129
01:31:32,720 --> 01:31:36,550
Well, you'd know all about the madness within, wouldn't you?

1130
01:31:46,770 --> 01:31:47,930
-I found him.   -I know.

1131
01:31:47,940 --> 01:31:49,430
-He's here.   -I understand.

1132
01:31:49,440 --> 01:31:52,840
-Let's kill him!   -No! I trusted you!

1133
01:31:53,080 --> 01:31:57,010
And all this time, you've been his friend.

1134
01:31:57,520 --> 01:32:00,770
He's a werewolf! That's why he's been missing classes.

1135
01:32:03,390 --> 01:32:05,280
How long have you known?

1136
01:32:05,590 --> 01:32:08,990
-Since Professor Snape set the essay.   -Well, Hermione.

1137
01:32:08,990 --> 01:32:12,090
You are the brightest witch of your age I've ever met.

1138
01:32:12,100 --> 01:32:14,700
Enough talk, Remus! Come on, let's kill him!

1139
01:32:14,700 --> 01:32:17,490
-Wait!   -I did my waiting!

1140
01:32:17,500 --> 01:32:20,140
Twelve years of it!

1141
01:32:20,540 --> 01:32:23,140
In Azkaban!

1142
01:32:32,420 --> 01:32:34,350
Very well. Kill him.

1143
01:32:34,720 --> 01:32:38,650
But wait one more minute. Harry has the right to know why.

1144
01:32:38,660 --> 01:32:40,410
I know why.

1145
01:32:40,460 --> 01:32:42,850
You betrayed my parents.

1146
01:32:42,860 --> 01:32:44,440
-You're the reason they're dead!

1147
01:32:44,450 --> 01:32:45,950
-No, it wasn't him.

1148
01:32:45,960 --> 01:32:48,020
Somebody did betray your parents...

1149
01:32:48,030 --> 01:32:51,720
...somebody who, until quite recently, I believed to be dead!

1150
01:32:51,740 --> 01:32:55,360
-Who was it, then?   -Peter Pettigrew!

1151
01:32:55,370 --> 01:32:58,700
And he's in this room! Right now!

1152
01:32:59,010 --> 01:33:02,140
Come out, come out, Peter!

1153
01:33:02,150 --> 01:33:05,340
-Come out, come out and play!   -Expelliarmus!

1154
01:33:08,090 --> 01:33:10,750
Vengeance is sweet.

1155
01:33:10,760 --> 01:33:13,180
How I hoped I'd be the one to catch you.

1156
01:33:13,190 --> 01:33:14,680
Severus...

1157
01:33:14,690 --> 01:33:18,050
I told Dumbledore you were helping a friend into the castle.

1158
01:33:18,060 --> 01:33:19,590
Here's the proof.

1159
01:33:19,600 --> 01:33:21,090
Brilliant, Snape.

1160
01:33:21,100 --> 01:33:25,700
You put your keen mind to the task and come to the wrong conclusion.

1161
01:33:25,700 --> 01:33:28,530
If you'll excuse us, Remus and I have business...

1162
01:33:28,540 --> 01:33:33,700
-...to attend to.   -Give me a reason. I beg you!

1163
01:33:33,710 --> 01:33:36,470
-Don't be a fool.   -He can't help it. It's habit.

1164
01:33:36,510 --> 01:33:38,240
-Be quiet.   -Be quiet yourself!

1165
01:33:38,250 --> 01:33:40,840
You two, quarrelling like an old married couple.

1166
01:33:40,850 --> 01:33:43,580
Run along and play with your chemistry set!

1167
01:33:43,920 --> 01:33:46,610
I could do it, you know.

1168
01:33:46,890 --> 01:33:52,690
But why deny the dementors? They're so longing to see you.

1169
01:33:52,700 --> 01:33:55,560
Do I detect a flicker of fear? Oh, yes.

1170
01:33:55,570 --> 01:33:59,230
A Dementor's Kiss. One can only imagine what that must be like.

1171
01:33:59,240 --> 01:34:02,760
It's said to be nearly unbearable to witness,

1172
01:34:02,770 --> 01:34:04,840
but I'll do my best.

1173
01:34:04,880 --> 01:34:07,310
Severus, please.

1174
01:34:08,150 --> 01:34:10,340
After you.

1175
01:34:14,590 --> 01:34:16,510
Expelliarmus!

1176
01:34:18,090 --> 01:34:20,070
-Harry! What did you just do?

1177
01:34:20,080 --> 01:34:21,850
-You attacked a teacher!

1178
01:34:21,890 --> 01:34:24,620
-Tell me about Peter.   -He was at school with us.

1179
01:34:24,630 --> 01:34:26,450
We thought he was our friend!

1180
01:34:26,460 --> 01:34:28,560
-No. Pettigrew's dead. You killed him!

1181
01:34:28,570 --> 01:34:29,620
-No, he didn't.

1182
01:34:29,630 --> 01:34:30,850
I thought so too,

1183
01:34:30,860 --> 01:34:33,030
until you mentioned Pettigrew on the map!

1184
01:34:33,070 --> 01:34:36,030
-The map was lying, then.   -The map never lies!

1185
01:34:36,040 --> 01:34:40,230
Pettigrew's alive! And he's right there!

1186
01:34:40,480 --> 01:34:45,270
-Me?! He's mental!   -Not you! Your rat!

1187
01:34:45,350 --> 01:34:48,640
-Scabbers has been in my family for...   -Twelve years?

1188
01:34:48,650 --> 01:34:51,310
Curiously long life for a common garden rat!

1189
01:34:51,320 --> 01:34:54,080
-He's missing a toe, isn't he?   -So what?

1190
01:34:54,090 --> 01:34:56,210
-All they could find of Pettigrew was his...

1191
01:34:56,220 --> 01:34:57,260
-Finger!

1192
01:34:57,260 --> 01:34:58,980
Dirty coward cut it off so

1193
01:34:58,990 --> 01:35:00,650
everyone would think he was dead!

1194
01:35:00,660 --> 01:35:03,890
-And then he transformed into a rat!   -Show me.

1195
01:35:06,300 --> 01:35:09,560
-Give it to him, Ron.   -What are you trying to do to him?

1196
01:35:09,570 --> 01:35:10,800
Scabbers!

1197
01:35:10,810 --> 01:35:14,070
Leave him alone! Get off him! What are you doing?

1198
01:35:36,370 --> 01:35:38,400
Remus?

1199
01:35:38,970 --> 01:35:40,630
Sirius.

1200
01:35:40,640 --> 01:35:42,740
My old friends!

1201
01:35:48,180 --> 01:35:52,170
Harry! Look at you. You look so much like your father.

1202
01:35:52,180 --> 01:35:54,060
-James. We were the best of friends...

1203
01:35:54,070 --> 01:35:56,050
-How dare you speak to Harry!

1204
01:35:56,690 --> 01:35:59,520
How dare you talk about James in front of him!

1205
01:35:59,520 --> 01:36:03,110
-You sold James and Lily to Voldemort!

1206
01:36:03,120 --> 01:36:04,890
-I didn't mean to!

1207
01:36:04,900 --> 01:36:05,790
The Dark Lord.

1208
01:36:05,800 --> 01:36:07,930
You have no idea the weapons he possesses!

1209
01:36:07,930 --> 01:36:10,760
Ask yourself, Sirius! What would you have done?

1210
01:36:10,940 --> 01:36:12,790
-What would you have done?

1211
01:36:12,800 --> 01:36:16,730
-Died, rather than betray my friends!

1212
01:36:18,710 --> 01:36:21,270
James wouldn't have wanted me killed!

1213
01:36:21,280 --> 01:36:27,140
Your dad would have spared me! He would have shown me mercy!

1214
01:36:27,450 --> 01:36:29,540
Should have realized if Voldemort didn't kill you,

1215
01:36:29,550 --> 01:36:31,850
we would. Together!

1216
01:36:31,860 --> 01:36:34,080
No!

1217
01:36:35,390 --> 01:36:39,520
-Harry, this man...   -I know what he is.

1218
01:36:39,530 --> 01:36:41,590
But we'll take him to the castle.

1219
01:36:41,600 --> 01:36:46,860
-Bless you, boy. Bless you!   -Get off!

1220
01:36:47,800 --> 01:36:50,400
I said we'd take you to the castle.

1221
01:36:50,570 --> 01:36:52,970
After that, the dementors can have you.

1222
01:36:56,710 --> 01:37:00,610
Sorry about my bite. I wake a trip with pain a bit.

1223
01:37:00,620 --> 01:37:04,310
A bit? A bit? You almost tore my leg off!

1224
01:37:04,320 --> 01:37:06,050
I was going for the rat.

1225
01:37:06,060 --> 01:37:10,050
Normally, I have a very sweet disposition as a dog.

1226
01:37:10,060 --> 01:37:15,460
More than once, James suggested that I make the change permanent.

1227
01:37:15,470 --> 01:37:17,790
The tail I could live with.

1228
01:37:17,800 --> 01:37:20,530
But the fleas, they're murder.

1229
01:37:32,920 --> 01:37:34,610
Okay.

1230
01:37:39,420 --> 01:37:42,120
-You better go.   -No. Don't worry, okay?

1231
01:37:42,130 --> 01:37:43,720
It's fine. I'll stay.

1232
01:37:44,290 --> 01:37:46,480
You go, I'll stay.

1233
01:37:46,600 --> 01:37:49,920
-You okay?   -I'm fine. Go.

1234
01:37:51,300 --> 01:37:54,460
-That looks really painful.   -So painful.

1235
01:37:54,470 --> 01:37:57,230
They might chop it.

1236
01:37:57,510 --> 01:38:00,330
I'm sure Madam Pomfrey will fix it in a heartbeat.

1237
01:38:00,340 --> 01:38:04,740
It's too late. It's ruined. It'll have to be chopped off.

1238
01:38:05,820 --> 01:38:07,850
It's beautiful, isn't it?

1239
01:38:08,490 --> 01:38:12,450
I'll never forget the first time I walked through those doors.

1240
01:38:12,960 --> 01:38:16,320
It'll be nice to do it again as a free man.

1241
01:38:18,260 --> 01:38:21,260
That was a noble thing you did back there.

1242
01:38:21,870 --> 01:38:24,190
He doesn't deserve it.

1243
01:38:24,200 --> 01:38:27,530
I didn't think my dad would have wanted his best friends...

1244
01:38:27,540 --> 01:38:29,260
...to become killers.

1245
01:38:29,270 --> 01:38:33,130
Besides, dead, the truth dies with him.

1246
01:38:33,140 --> 01:38:35,670
Alive, you're free.

1247
01:38:35,680 --> 01:38:38,970
Turn me into a flobberworm. Anything but the dementors!

1248
01:38:38,980 --> 01:38:41,100
Ron! Haven't I been a good pet?

1249
01:38:41,110 --> 01:38:42,480
You won't let them give me...

1250
01:38:42,490 --> 01:38:45,150
...to the dementors, will you? I was your rat!

1251
01:38:45,160 --> 01:38:48,080
-Sweet, clever girl! Surely you won't...

1252
01:38:48,090 --> 01:38:49,380
-Get away from her!

1253
01:38:51,660 --> 01:38:53,720
I don't know if you know, Harry...

1254
01:38:53,730 --> 01:38:57,990
...but when you were born, James and Lily made me your godfather.

1255
01:38:58,000 --> 01:39:00,130
I know.

1256
01:39:01,100 --> 01:39:05,330
I can understand if you choose to stay with your aunt and uncle...

1257
01:39:05,340 --> 01:39:08,000
...but if you ever wanted a different home....

1258
01:39:08,010 --> 01:39:10,700
What? Come and live with you?

1259
01:39:11,820 --> 01:39:15,110
It's just a thought. I can understand if you don't want to.

1260
01:39:15,120 --> 01:39:17,080
Harry!

1261
01:39:32,130 --> 01:39:36,030
Remus, my old friend. Have you taken your potion tonight?

1262
01:39:37,140 --> 01:39:40,070
You know the man you truly are, Remus!

1263
01:39:40,080 --> 01:39:42,670
This heart is where you truly live! Here!

1264
01:39:43,850 --> 01:39:46,040
This flesh is only flesh!

1265
01:39:46,980 --> 01:39:49,270
Expelliarmus!

1266
01:39:59,160 --> 01:40:00,920
Harry!

1267
01:40:01,800 --> 01:40:04,970
Remus! Remus!

1268
01:40:10,970 --> 01:40:13,500
Run! Run!

1269
01:40:23,320 --> 01:40:25,510
-Come on.   -Wait. Wait.

1270
01:40:25,520 --> 01:40:30,780
Hermione! Bad idea. Bad idea.

1271
01:40:30,790 --> 01:40:33,220
Professor?

1272
01:40:37,130 --> 01:40:38,860
Professor Lupin?

1273
01:40:46,440 --> 01:40:49,870
Nice doggy. Nice doggy!

1274
01:40:50,110 --> 01:40:52,840
There you are, Potter!

1275
01:41:26,450 --> 01:41:27,670
Sirius!

1276
01:41:28,320 --> 01:41:30,920
Come back here, Potter!

1277
01:42:36,550 --> 01:42:38,150
Sirius!

1278
01:42:38,760 --> 01:42:41,920
No. Sirius!

1279
01:43:23,600 --> 01:43:26,670
Expecto Patronum!

1280
01:45:39,270 --> 01:45:41,830
Harry?

1281
01:45:42,570 --> 01:45:45,140
I saw my dad.

1282
01:45:45,140 --> 01:45:46,900
What?

1283
01:45:46,910 --> 01:45:48,600
He sent the dementors away.

1284
01:45:48,610 --> 01:45:50,210
I saw him across the lake.

1285
01:45:50,210 --> 01:45:52,040
Harry, they've captured Sirius.

1286
01:45:52,080 --> 01:45:55,070
Any minute the dementors are gonna perform the Kiss.

1287
01:45:55,080 --> 01:45:57,770
-They're gonna kill him?   -No. It's worse.

1288
01:45:57,790 --> 01:45:59,780
Much worse.

1289
01:45:59,790 --> 01:46:02,350
They're going to suck out his soul.

1290
01:46:03,860 --> 01:46:05,420
Headmaster, stop them.

1291
01:46:05,430 --> 01:46:06,680
-They've got the wrong man.

1292
01:46:06,690 --> 01:46:08,950
-It's true. Sirius is innocent.

1293
01:46:08,960 --> 01:46:11,320
-It's Scabbers who did it.   -Scabbers?

1294
01:46:11,330 --> 01:46:12,930
He's my rat, sir.

1295
01:46:13,130 --> 01:46:15,420
He's not really a rat. He was a rat.

1296
01:46:15,430 --> 01:46:17,130
He was my brother Percy's rat.

1297
01:46:17,140 --> 01:46:19,200
-But then they gave him an owl...

1298
01:46:19,210 --> 01:46:21,000
-The point is, we know the truth.

1299
01:46:21,010 --> 01:46:23,700
-Please believe us.   -I do, Miss Granger.

1300
01:46:23,740 --> 01:46:29,350
But the word of three 13-year-old wizards will convince few others.

1301
01:46:32,250 --> 01:46:35,180
A child's voice, however honest and true...

1302
01:46:35,190 --> 01:46:39,150
...is meaningless to those who have forgotten how to listen.

1303
01:46:44,170 --> 01:46:46,890
Mysterious thing, time.

1304
01:46:47,870 --> 01:46:49,360
Powerful...

1305
01:46:49,370 --> 01:46:52,470
...and when meddled with, dangerous.

1306
01:46:53,840 --> 01:46:57,670
Sirius Black is in the topmost cell of the Dark Tower.

1307
01:46:58,280 --> 01:47:00,540
You know the laws, Miss Granger.

1308
01:47:00,550 --> 01:47:02,510
You must not be seen.

1309
01:47:02,520 --> 01:47:06,340
And you would do well, I feel, to return before this last chime.

1310
01:47:06,350 --> 01:47:10,080
If not, the consequences are too ghastly to discuss.

1311
01:47:10,420 --> 01:47:12,380
If you succeed tonight...

1312
01:47:12,390 --> 01:47:15,430
...more than one innocent life may be spared.

1313
01:47:17,060 --> 01:47:19,490
Three turns should do it, I think.

1314
01:47:24,170 --> 01:47:26,160
Oh, and by the way.

1315
01:47:26,170 --> 01:47:32,170
When in doubt, I find retracing my steps to be a wise place to begin.

1316
01:47:32,180 --> 01:47:34,440
Good luck.

1317
01:47:34,750 --> 01:47:37,420
What the bloody hell was that all about?

1318
01:47:37,890 --> 01:47:40,420
Sorry, Ron, but seeing as you can't walk....

1319
01:48:09,220 --> 01:48:10,980
What just happened?

1320
01:48:10,990 --> 01:48:13,440
-Where's Ron?   -7:30.

1321
01:48:13,450 --> 01:48:15,480
Where were we at 7:30?

1322
01:48:15,490 --> 01:48:17,450
I don't know. Going to Hagrid's?

1323
01:48:17,460 --> 01:48:20,060
Come on. And we can't be seen.

1324
01:48:20,930 --> 01:48:22,960
Hermione!

1325
01:48:40,950 --> 01:48:43,810
Hermione! Hermione, wait.

1326
01:48:45,420 --> 01:48:49,180
Hermione, will you please tell me what it is we're doing?

1327
01:48:49,190 --> 01:48:52,180
You foul, loathsome, evil little cockroach!

1328
01:48:52,190 --> 01:48:53,720
That's us.

1329
01:48:53,760 --> 01:48:56,860
Hermione, no! He's not worth it.

1330
01:48:56,900 --> 01:48:58,530
This is not normal.

1331
01:49:00,630 --> 01:49:03,160
This is a Time-Turner, Harry.

1332
01:49:03,170 --> 01:49:05,530
McGonagall gave it to me first term.

1333
01:49:05,540 --> 01:49:09,110
This is how I've been getting to my lessons all year.

1334
01:49:09,110 --> 01:49:12,470
-You mean we've gone back in time?   -Yes.

1335
01:49:12,480 --> 01:49:16,050
Dumbledore obviously wanted us to return to this moment.

1336
01:49:18,150 --> 01:49:21,510
Clearly, something happened he wants us to change.

1337
01:49:24,460 --> 01:49:25,950
Good punch.

1338
01:49:25,960 --> 01:49:27,650
Thanks.

1339
01:49:28,460 --> 01:49:30,320
Malfoy's coming.

1340
01:49:31,030 --> 01:49:33,560
-Run.   -Not a word to anyone, understood?

1341
01:49:33,830 --> 01:49:37,060
I'm gonna get that jumped-up mudblood! Mark my words.

1342
01:49:37,070 --> 01:49:41,210
-That felt good.   -Not good, brilliant.

1343
01:49:42,380 --> 01:49:45,170
Come on. We should be at Hagrid's.

1344
01:50:04,100 --> 01:50:06,860
Look. Buckbeak's still alive.

1345
01:50:08,100 --> 01:50:10,160
Of course.

1346
01:50:10,170 --> 01:50:12,330
Remember what Dumbledore said?

1347
01:50:12,340 --> 01:50:16,570
If we succeed, more than one innocent life could be spared.

1348
01:50:16,740 --> 01:50:18,270
Let's go.

1349
01:50:39,370 --> 01:50:41,630
Here they come. I'd better hurry.

1350
01:50:41,640 --> 01:50:44,290
Fudge has to see Buckbeak before we steal him.

1351
01:50:44,300 --> 01:50:46,970
Otherwise, he'll think Hagrid set him free.

1352
01:50:47,810 --> 01:50:50,370
Scabbers, you're alive!

1353
01:50:50,380 --> 01:50:53,340
-Keep a closer eye on your pet.   -That's Pettigrew.

1354
01:50:53,380 --> 01:50:56,440
-Harry, you can't.   -He betrayed my parents.

1355
01:50:56,450 --> 01:50:59,640
-You don't expect me to sit here.   -Yes, and you must!

1356
01:51:03,320 --> 01:51:06,220
Harry, you're in Hagrid's hut now.

1357
01:51:06,230 --> 01:51:09,220
If you go bursting in, you'll think you've gone mad.

1358
01:51:09,230 --> 01:51:12,260
Awful things happen to wizards who meddle with time.

1359
01:51:12,270 --> 01:51:14,730
We can't be seen.

1360
01:51:17,800 --> 01:51:19,730
Fudge is coming.

1361
01:51:20,440 --> 01:51:22,730
And we aren't leaving?

1362
01:51:24,680 --> 01:51:26,470
Why aren't we leaving?

1363
01:51:37,190 --> 01:51:38,950
Are you mad?

1364
01:51:44,760 --> 01:51:46,330
That hurt.

1365
01:51:46,330 --> 01:51:47,860
Sorry.

1366
01:52:08,520 --> 01:52:11,380
We're coming out the back door. Go!

1367
01:52:28,610 --> 01:52:31,610
Is that really what my hair looks like from the back?

1368
01:52:33,480 --> 01:52:35,010
What?

1369
01:52:35,680 --> 01:52:37,710
I thought I just saw....

1370
01:52:37,720 --> 01:52:40,580
-Never mind.   -Let's go.

1371
01:52:54,700 --> 01:52:57,200
Okay, go, Harry. Go!

1372
01:53:03,240 --> 01:53:05,410
Get away. Get off.

1373
01:53:27,400 --> 01:53:31,000
Minister, I really think I should sign as well.

1374
01:53:31,670 --> 01:53:35,000
Yes, very well. Perhaps it would be....

1375
01:53:35,040 --> 01:53:39,010
Okay, Buckbeak. Come quickly. Come with us now. Come on.

1376
01:53:43,280 --> 01:53:46,180
Keep trying. Come on. Quickly.

1377
01:53:48,390 --> 01:53:52,390
Buckbeak. Okay? Quickly. Hurry up. Okay?

1378
01:53:52,990 --> 01:53:56,490
-Your name only.   -It's such a very long name....

1379
01:53:56,700 --> 01:53:58,590
Hurry up now, Buckbeak, okay?

1380
01:54:01,100 --> 01:54:04,270
Come on. Come on, Buckbeak.

1381
01:54:04,270 --> 01:54:06,770
Come and get the nice dead ferret.

1382
01:54:09,210 --> 01:54:11,580
-Come on. It's here. Come on, Beaky.

1383
01:54:11,590 --> 01:54:13,900
-Here we are, minister. Follow me.

1384
01:54:13,910 --> 01:54:15,770
-Now, look there.   -Where?

1385
01:54:15,780 --> 01:54:19,310
-Look beyond the rocks.   -What am I supposed to see?

1386
01:54:19,320 --> 01:54:22,980
Professor Dippet had that ling planted when he was headmaster.

1387
01:54:22,990 --> 01:54:26,020
-Oh, yes. Indeed, indeed.   -And all the strawberries.

1388
01:54:26,790 --> 01:54:29,820
-Come on, Buckbeak. Come on.   -I see no strawberries.

1389
01:54:29,830 --> 01:54:31,150
-Over there.   -Where?

1390
01:54:31,160 --> 01:54:33,130
-Over there.   -This way.

1391
01:54:33,130 --> 01:54:35,990
-Let's get this over, please.   -All right.

1392
01:54:37,470 --> 01:54:39,360
But where is it?

1393
01:54:40,110 --> 01:54:42,500
I saw the beast, just now.

1394
01:54:42,940 --> 01:54:45,300
-Not a moment ago!   -How extraordinary.

1395
01:54:45,310 --> 01:54:46,840
Buckbeak.

1396
01:54:46,850 --> 01:54:51,110
Come now, Dumbledore. Someone's obviously released him.

1397
01:54:51,120 --> 01:54:52,650
-Hagrid?   -Buckbeak.

1398
01:54:52,650 --> 01:54:57,080
I don't think the minister's suggesting you had anything to do with this.

1399
01:54:57,120 --> 01:55:00,120
How could you? You've been with us all the time.

1400
01:55:00,130 --> 01:55:02,150
-Right.   -Well, well....

1401
01:55:02,160 --> 01:55:03,850
We must search the grounds.

1402
01:55:03,860 --> 01:55:07,060
Well, search the skies, if you must, minister.

1403
01:55:07,070 --> 01:55:12,660
Meanwhile, I'd like a nice cup of tea or a large brandy.

1404
01:55:12,670 --> 01:55:16,830
Oh, executioner, your services are no longer required.

1405
01:55:16,840 --> 01:55:18,910
Thank you.

1406
01:55:18,910 --> 01:55:22,410
You'll find no small glasses in this house, professor.

1407
01:55:32,990 --> 01:55:34,680
-Come on.   -This way.

1408
01:55:41,300 --> 01:55:43,260
This way, now.

1409
01:55:45,500 --> 01:55:47,430
-Now what?   -We save Sirius.

1410
01:55:47,440 --> 01:55:50,130
-How?   -No idea.

1411
01:55:59,250 --> 01:56:01,820
-Look. It's Lupin.   -Immobulus!

1412
01:56:08,060 --> 01:56:10,250
And Snape's coming.

1413
01:56:16,270 --> 01:56:18,130
And now we wait.

1414
01:56:19,140 --> 01:56:21,130
And now we wait.

1415
01:56:48,500 --> 01:56:51,960
-At least someone's enjoying himself.   -Yeah.

1416
01:56:54,570 --> 01:56:56,500
-Hermione?   -Yeah?

1417
01:56:56,510 --> 01:57:01,000
Before, down by the lake, when I was with Sirius...

1418
01:57:01,010 --> 01:57:03,310
...I did see someone.

1419
01:57:03,320 --> 01:57:06,910
That someone made the dementors go away.

1420
01:57:06,920 --> 01:57:08,410
With a Patronus.

1421
01:57:08,420 --> 01:57:10,480
I heard Snape telling Dumbledore.

1422
01:57:10,490 --> 01:57:12,110
According to him...

1423
01:57:12,120 --> 01:57:15,680
...only a really powerful wizard could have conjured it.

1424
01:57:15,690 --> 01:57:17,790
It was my dad.

1425
01:57:18,700 --> 01:57:20,660
My dad conjured the Patronus.

1426
01:57:20,670 --> 01:57:23,130
-Harry, but your dad's...   -Dead. I know.

1427
01:57:24,340 --> 01:57:26,870
I'm just telling you what I saw.

1428
01:57:30,810 --> 01:57:32,640
Here we come.

1429
01:57:38,120 --> 01:57:40,640
You see Sirius talking to me there?

1430
01:57:40,650 --> 01:57:43,750
-He's asking me to come live with him.   -That's great.

1431
01:57:43,760 --> 01:57:47,150
When we free him, I'll never have to go back to the Dursleys'.

1432
01:57:47,160 --> 01:57:48,980
It'll just be me and him.

1433
01:57:49,460 --> 01:57:51,550
We could live in the country...

1434
01:57:51,560 --> 01:57:54,360
...someplace you can see the sky.

1435
01:57:54,370 --> 01:57:57,400
He'll like that after all those years in Azkaban.

1436
01:57:58,240 --> 01:57:59,990
Harry!

1437
01:58:01,340 --> 01:58:03,230
Run!

1438
01:58:09,950 --> 01:58:11,670
Let's go.

1439
01:58:31,040 --> 01:58:33,570
-What are you doing?   -Saving your life.

1440
01:58:37,610 --> 01:58:39,210
Thanks.

1441
01:58:40,850 --> 01:58:42,850
-Great. Now he's coming for us.

1442
01:58:42,860 --> 01:58:45,070
-Yeah, I didn't think about that. Run!

1443
01:59:59,990 --> 02:00:01,920
That was so scary.

1444
02:00:01,930 --> 02:00:05,060
Poor Professor Lupin's having a really tough night.

1445
02:00:16,310 --> 02:00:19,630
Sirius. Come on!

1446
02:00:35,460 --> 02:00:37,720
-This is horrible.   -Don't worry.

1447
02:00:37,730 --> 02:00:41,160
My dad will come. He'll conjure the Patronus.

1448
02:00:49,670 --> 02:00:51,700
Any minute now.

1449
02:00:51,710 --> 02:00:53,930
Right there. You'll see.

1450
02:00:55,150 --> 02:00:57,800
Harry, listen to me. No one's coming.

1451
02:00:57,810 --> 02:01:00,540
Don't worry, he will. He will come.

1452
02:01:04,490 --> 02:01:07,120
-Sirius.   -You're dying...

1453
02:01:08,990 --> 02:01:11,060
...both of you.

1454
02:01:12,930 --> 02:01:14,860
Harry!

1455
02:01:16,570 --> 02:01:20,630
Expecto Patronum!

1456
02:02:19,060 --> 02:02:20,790
You were right, Hermione.

1457
02:02:20,800 --> 02:02:24,290
It wasn't my dad I saw earlier. It was me!

1458
02:02:24,300 --> 02:02:27,230
I saw myself conjuring the Patronus before.

1459
02:02:27,240 --> 02:02:29,760
I knew I could do it this time because...

1460
02:02:29,770 --> 02:02:31,630
...well, I had already done it.

1461
02:02:31,640 --> 02:02:34,270
-Does that make sense?   -No.

1462
02:02:34,280 --> 02:02:37,310
But I don't like flying...!

1463
02:02:50,260 --> 02:02:51,790
Bombarda!

1464
02:03:24,900 --> 02:03:27,850
I'll be forever grateful for this...

1465
02:03:27,860 --> 02:03:29,360
...to both of you.

1466
02:03:29,370 --> 02:03:32,460
-I want to go with you.   -One day, perhaps.

1467
02:03:32,470 --> 02:03:35,530
For some time, my life will be too unpredictable.

1468
02:03:35,540 --> 02:03:37,500
And besides...

1469
02:03:38,210 --> 02:03:41,670
-...you're meant to be here.   -But you're innocent.

1470
02:03:41,680 --> 02:03:44,000
And you know it.

1471
02:03:44,880 --> 02:03:46,980
And for now, that will do.

1472
02:03:49,090 --> 02:03:51,840
I expect you're tired of hearing this...

1473
02:03:52,660 --> 02:03:55,380
...but you look so like your father.

1474
02:03:56,930 --> 02:03:59,090
Except your eyes.

1475
02:03:59,860 --> 02:04:02,360
-You have...   -My mother's eyes.

1476
02:04:04,100 --> 02:04:07,090
It's cruel that I spent so much time with James and Lily,

1477
02:04:07,100 --> 02:04:09,400
and you so little.

1478
02:04:09,810 --> 02:04:11,490
But know this:

1479
02:04:12,410 --> 02:04:15,770
The ones that love us never really leave us.

1480
02:04:16,950 --> 02:04:19,110
And you can always find them...

1481
02:04:21,320 --> 02:04:23,380
...in here.

1482
02:04:33,560 --> 02:04:36,290
You really are the brightest witch of your age.

1483
02:05:02,930 --> 02:05:04,750
We have to go.

1484
02:05:32,820 --> 02:05:35,650
-Well?   -He's free. We did it.

1485
02:05:35,660 --> 02:05:37,380
Did what?

1486
02:05:37,390 --> 02:05:39,530
Good night.

1487
02:05:48,100 --> 02:05:49,600
How did you get there?

1488
02:05:49,610 --> 02:05:51,100
I was talking to you there.

1489
02:05:51,110 --> 02:05:52,470
And now you're there.

1490
02:05:52,610 --> 02:05:55,400
-What's he talking about, Harry?   -I don't know.

1491
02:05:55,410 --> 02:05:56,720
Honestly, Ron.

1492
02:05:56,730 --> 02:05:59,140
How can somebody be in two places at once?

1493
02:06:25,440 --> 02:06:27,130
Hello, Harry.

1494
02:06:30,550 --> 02:06:32,580
I saw you coming.

1495
02:06:36,950 --> 02:06:39,850
I've looked worse, believe me.

1496
02:06:42,360 --> 02:06:45,690
-You've been sacked.   -No.

1497
02:06:45,700 --> 02:06:48,820
No. I resigned, actually.

1498
02:06:48,830 --> 02:06:50,760
Resigned? Why?

1499
02:06:50,770 --> 02:06:56,230
Well, it seems that somebody let slip the nature of my condition.

1500
02:06:56,240 --> 02:06:58,140
This time tomorrow,

1501
02:06:58,150 --> 02:07:01,900
the owls will start arriving and parents will not want...

1502
02:07:01,910 --> 02:07:05,480
...well, someone like me teaching their children.

1503
02:07:05,510 --> 02:07:07,570
-But Dumbledore...   -He has already...

1504
02:07:07,580 --> 02:07:09,610
...risked enough on my behalf.

1505
02:07:09,620 --> 02:07:13,080
Besides, people like me are....

1506
02:07:13,520 --> 02:07:17,050
Well, let's just say that I'm used to it by now.

1507
02:07:26,400 --> 02:07:29,130
Why do you look so miserable, Harry?

1508
02:07:29,140 --> 02:07:31,500
None of it made any difference.

1509
02:07:31,510 --> 02:07:35,200
-Pettigrew escaped.   -Didn't make any difference?

1510
02:07:35,210 --> 02:07:38,870
It made all the difference in the world. You uncovered the truth.

1511
02:07:38,880 --> 02:07:41,570
You saved an innocent man from a terrible fate.

1512
02:07:41,750 --> 02:07:44,440
It made a great deal of difference.

1513
02:07:48,890 --> 02:07:51,250
If I am proud of anything...

1514
02:07:51,260 --> 02:07:54,090
...it is of how much you have learned this year.

1515
02:07:54,100 --> 02:07:57,030
Now, since I am no longer your teacher...

1516
02:07:57,030 --> 02:08:01,460
...I feel no guilt whatsoever about giving this back to you.

1517
02:08:02,170 --> 02:08:04,830
So now I'll say goodbye, Harry.

1518
02:08:04,840 --> 02:08:07,630
I feel sure we'll meet again sometime.

1519
02:08:07,980 --> 02:08:09,510
Until then...

1520
02:08:10,650 --> 02:08:12,540
...mischief managed.

1521
02:08:46,610 --> 02:08:48,800
Stand back, I said!

1522
02:08:48,810 --> 02:08:50,980
Or I'll take it upstairs if you don't settle.

1523
02:08:50,990 --> 02:08:52,580
Harry.

1524
02:08:53,220 --> 02:08:54,780
Wherever did you get it?

1525
02:08:54,790 --> 02:08:57,350
Can I have a go, Harry? After you, of course.

1526
02:08:57,360 --> 02:08:59,680
-What are you talking about?   -Quiet.

1527
02:08:59,690 --> 02:09:03,150
Let the man through. I didn't mean to open it, Harry.

1528
02:09:03,160 --> 02:09:05,820
It was badly wrapped. They made me do it.

1529
02:09:05,830 --> 02:09:07,520
Did not.

1530
02:09:08,700 --> 02:09:12,360
-It's a Firebolt.   -It's the fastest broom in the world.

1531
02:09:12,370 --> 02:09:14,100
For me?

1532
02:09:14,110 --> 02:09:16,800
